window.AKK_FORENSIC_PSYCHOLOGICAL_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_FORENSIC_PSYCHOLOGICAL_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":201,"title":"Chapter 201: The Case of the Split-Brain Patient: An Accident","paragraphs":["Mu Mian practically half-carried Chen Xue into the car. Fang Rui drove in front, and together they headed to the hospital to check on Zhang.","The heavy rain showed no signs of stopping, pattering noisily against the car windows, creating a foggy haze that blurred the road ahead.","By the time they arrived at the hospital, Zhang's parents were already there. They had signed the surgical consent form, and Zhang had been rushed into the operating room for emergency treatment.","Chen Xue hadn’t brought an umbrella. She had run through the rain to get here, her clothes completely soaked.","Zhang’s mother, seeing how drenched she was, quickly handed her own coat to Chen Xue.","But Chen Xue didn’t take it. She seemed lost in her own world, staring fixedly at the red light above the operating room door.","“Auntie, how is Zhang doing?” Fang Rui asked.","Zhang’s mother wiped her tears and choked back a sob. “The doctor said the situation is very grim. Zhang Qiang’s head injury is severe, and they’re not sure if they can save him. They told us to prepare for the worst...”","Director Liu had also been severely injured in the accident. His injuries were even more critical, and by the time he was brought to the hospital, he had already passed away.","Mu Mian, as if trying to comfort them or perhaps praying, said, “Officer Zhang will be fine.”","The red light above the operating room remained lit. Inside, the doctors were doing everything they could to save him, while those waiting outside were consumed with anxiety.","Fang Rui leaned against the wall in the hallway, filled with guilt. If he hadn’t sent Zhang to follow Director Liu, this accident might never have happened. But years of professional training didn’t allow him to show any sign of weakness.","Once, he had been a talkative and clever young officer like Zhang. But as his older colleagues retired or fell in the line of duty, he had risen to become a captain, forced to mature and shoulder the responsibilities that came with it.","This wasn’t the first time he had seen a colleague seriously injured, and he knew it wouldn’t be the last. In their line of work, injuries and sacrifices were all too common.","But this time, it was his partner.","Zhang might have seemed unreliable at times, but his personality made it easier for him to connect with people during investigations. In their work, he and Zhang had formed a complementary partnership.","Mu Mian noticed that she couldn’t read the expressions on everyone’s faces. No one was crying, but the air was thick with an overwhelming sadness that refused to dissipate.","She took Fang Rui’s hand and noticed it was trembling. Fang Rui was afraid, but why? He was always so brave.","Tears welled up in Mu Mian’s eyes. Although Officer Zhang was only fourth on her list of close friends, he was a very special one.","He treated her like a normal person, joked with her, teased her about her quirks, and even took great care of her pet white mice.","Fang Rui pulled Mu Mian into his arms and comforted her, “He’ll be okay.”","“Fang Rui, I’m scared...”","She had so few friends. She couldn’t bear to lose another.","Zhang’s mother turned to Fang Rui and said, “Fang Rui, you two should go back to work. We’ll stay here and keep watch.”","Zhang’s father added, “Yes, there’s no need for all of us to stay. Zhang was following a suspect when the accident happened. This might not have been an accident at all. You should go investigate. We’ll stay here and let you know if anything changes.”","Fang Rui slowly composed himself. Zhang’s parents were right—this might not have been an accident. He needed to get to the bottom of it and find out who was really behind it.","Fang Rui and Mu Mian drove to the scene of the accident. The rain had lightened, but the sky remained dark and heavy.","Fang Rui had also sent people to seal off Director Liu’s home and office to prevent anyone from tampering with evidence.","Mu Mian analyzed, “It seemed like Officer Zhang was trying to tell us who the killer was. Could that be why the killer caused the accident, to silence him?”","Fang Rui replied, “Causing an accident requires timing. It couldn’t have been random—this was planned. But Zhang must have stumbled upon something by chance.","Director Liu’s injuries were more severe, which suggests he was the primary target. But if the killer really wanted to eliminate Director Liu, why wait until we were closing in? And why lead us to investigate him in the first place?”","“Could it be that the person who caused the accident isn’t the same person who disposed of the body? Maybe someone else is trying to stop us from investigating further?”","“That’s possible.”","The accident had taken place on the road outside Jiangzhou University Second Affiliated Hospital.","Mu Mian looked at the familiar sign and remembered that Chen Shu worked at this hospital.","She wondered aloud, “Why did Zhang suddenly say he knew who the killer was? What clue did he find?”","They had been to this hospital before during the investigation. Zhang knew some of the doctors and nurses there, so it was possible the killer was someone who worked at the hospital.","The accident site had already been cordoned off by traffic police. The rain had washed away most of the bloodstains on the ground.","The wet pavement was littered with car debris and broken parts. Six or seven cars parked along the roadside had been damaged, and a large truck lay overturned on its side.","The white car Director Liu had been driving was flipped over, its tires pointing skyward, the body of the car completely wrecked. Zhang’s black car was in slightly better condition, but the front end was crushed, and the shattered windshield was smeared with blood.","The dashcams in both cars had been destroyed, but the memory cards were still intact. Using footage from the dashcams and nearby surveillance cameras, the traffic police had already determined the cause of the accident.","One of the traffic officers, Old Liu, recognized Fang Rui. “Captain Fang, what brings you here?”","“What caused the accident?”","Old Liu explained the situation. “The white car and the black car were both parked in the roadside parking area when a large truck suddenly lost control and plowed into the row of cars. The two drivers who were still in their vehicles were seriously injured. One died on the spot, and the other is in critical condition.”","“What about the truck driver?”","“We’ve taken him into custody. When we arrived at the scene, we noticed he reeked of alcohol. A breathalyzer test showed his blood alcohol level was 85mg/100ml—he was driving under the influence.”","Fang Rui asked, “Can I join you in questioning him?”","“Of course.”","The truck driver, Li Xinyu, was in his forties and an experienced driver. But in recent years, he had developed a gambling addiction, racking up significant debts. His wife had divorced him as a result.","He looked nervously at Fang Rui and Old Liu, stammering, “Officers, I... I didn’t mean to.”","“Look at your blood alcohol level—you were clearly driving under the influence. And those dark circles under your eyes? You were up all night drinking, weren’t you? This is a case of drunk driving and fatigue!”","“Officers, it’s my fault. Yesterday was my birthday, but no one was around to celebrate with me, so I drank alone and had too much. I wasn’t planning to drive today, but a regular customer needed a shipment delivered urgently. I thought I was sober enough, so I took the job. I didn’t expect the rain to make things worse, and that’s how the accident happened.","I tried to fix it. The truck was about to veer into oncoming traffic, so I yanked the wheel and crashed into the parking area. I thought no one was there, but two unlucky people had parked their cars and stayed inside.”","Old Liu slammed his hand on the table. “Unlucky? You hit them, and you’re blaming their bad luck?”","Li Xinyu slapped his own mouth. “It’s my fault. I shouldn’t have said that.”","Fang Rui said, “Give me the contact information for that customer of yours.”","“Officers, the accident was my fault, not my customer’s. He has nothing to do with this. You can’t go harassing him.”","“Just give it to me!”","“I won’t betray my customer.”","Fang Rui sneered, “There is no customer, is there? Tell me, who ordered you to crash into them?”","“Officers, you can’t accuse me like this! I admit I caused the accident, but it wasn’t intentional. I didn’t mean to kill anyone. I have insurance—it’ll cover the damages for their families. I’ll go to prison if I have to, but you can’t frame me for murder.”","“You’re deep in debt, aren’t you? You need money, don’t you?”","“Yes, I owe a lot of money, which is why I drove out in the heavy rain to transport goods. Officer, even though I desperately need money, I wouldn’t break the law just to make a profit. If you don’t believe me, you can check my bank account balance to see if I’ve received any payments.”","Li Xinyu stubbornly insisted that he was driving under the influence of alcohol, refusing to admit that he had accepted any money."]},{"number":202,"title":"Chapter 202: The Split-Brain Case: The Mastermind Behind the Scenes","paragraphs":["Mu Mian was waiting for Fang Rui in the lobby of the traffic police station. A female officer on duty handed her a cup of warm water.","Mu Mian held the cup with both hands, quietly watching the ripples that occasionally formed on the surface of the water.","“Young lady, what’s wrong?” the officer asked gently.","Mu Mian whispered, “I might lose a friend soon. I’m really sad. I don’t want him to die, but I can’t stop death.”","Just as the officer was about to comfort her, Mu Mian handed the cup back. “Could you add some cocoa powder for me? Or some sugar... I’d like something sweet.”","It seemed she didn’t need much comforting after all.","“How about coffee powder?” the officer offered.","Mu Mian shook her head. “No, life is already bitter enough. I don’t want coffee.”","“Alright then, wait a moment. I’ll ask my colleague for some milk tea powder.”","Mu Mian slowly sipped the overly sweet milk tea. Just then, she spotted Fang Rui and hurried over to him. “Did the driver confess who was behind this?”","“No, he insists it was just drunk driving.”","Mu Mian frowned. “I’ve always thought the standards for drunk driving aren’t flexible enough.”","“Why do you say that?”","“The human body can build tolerance to certain stimuli. People who drink regularly have a higher alcohol tolerance than those who don’t. So, even if someone’s blood alcohol level meets the legal limit, they might not actually be drunk. And for others, it’s the opposite.”","Fang Rui nodded. “His blood alcohol level was 85mg/100ml, just slightly over the limit. That can’t be a coincidence.”","By the time they left the traffic police station, it was already 11 p.m. The rain had stopped, but the night was still shrouded in a heavy mist.","Then, Zhang’s mother called.","“Fang Rui, Zhang Qiang’s surgery was successful, but he’ll need to stay in the ICU for a few more days before he’s out of danger. Don’t worry about him too much. Get some rest.”","Mu Mian could hear Zhang’s mother crying. She felt that Officer Zhang wasn’t as safe as they hoped.","“Auntie, what did the doctor say?”","“The doctor said... even if Zhang Qiang pulls through, he might end up in a vegetative state... How could someone so lively and talkative end up like this?”","“Auntie, Zhang Qiang will get better.”","After hanging up, Fang Rui and Mu Mian stood by the empty roadside for a long time, so long that the rain began to pour again.","Mu Mian had never feared death before. She saw it as an unchangeable law of nature, so she could face it calmly, whether it was her own or someone else’s.","But now, she felt a little afraid—not of death itself, but of its consequences. If she died, how heartbroken would her sister and Fang Rui be? Officer Zhang couldn’t grieve anymore, and Chen Xue might mourn her, or maybe not.","Suddenly, Mu Mian felt relieved that she didn’t have many friends. If she died, only a few people would be sad. Unlike Officer Zhang, who had so many friends and family mourning for him.","Fang Rui shielded Mu Mian’s head from the rain. “Mu Mian, it’s raining. Let’s go back.”","“Okay. Fang Rui, if you want to cry, you can. It’s okay to cry. Tears aren’t a sign of weakness—they just show how much you’re hurting.”","“Mm.”","After a moment, Mu Mian added, “Fang Rui, I won’t die so soon. I’ll try to live a long, long time. You can’t die quickly either.”","“Okay.”","Then Mu Mian thought of something else. They couldn’t possibly die at the same time. One of them would inevitably be left behind. One of them would end up alone.","Seeing the rain streaming down Fang Rui’s face, she swallowed her words.","The next day, Fang Rui and Mu Mian went to the home of the driver, Li Xinyu.","He was a local who used to own a house in the old town, but he sold it to pay off gambling debts. His parents and son had moved to a rented place in the urban village.","Fang Rui first asked Li Xinyu’s neighbors about him.","“That son of theirs is completely useless. He’s deep in debt, and not long ago, debt collectors were showing up at his door every day. It was terrifying.”","“Have they stopped coming recently?”","“It seems like they’ve stopped.”","“Has Li Xinyu’s financial situation improved?”","“It’s gotten much better. At least they can afford meat now. When they first moved here, his elderly mother would only buy cabbage. But for the past month, Li Xinyu’s been doing the shopping, buying fish and meat every day. I wonder where he got the money.”","“How’s his alcohol tolerance?”","“He can hold his liquor really well. He’s always drinking with his buddies at the street-side stalls downstairs. He can down several pounds of baijiu by himself!”","Fang Rui and Mu Mian went to Li Xinyu’s home. An elderly woman with graying hair and a hunched back opened the door.","When she learned why they were there, her expression changed. She went to a chest in the room and pulled out a bundle of money, handing it to Fang Rui. “Officer, my son must have committed a crime. This is the dirty money. I’m handing it over. Can you reduce his sentence?”","“Granny, how do you know this is dirty money?”","“I know my son. How else would he suddenly have so much money? He must have stolen it. I haven’t spent a single cent of it. Take it all.”","The bundle contained about twenty to thirty thousand yuan.","Just then, Mu Mian received a report.","“Fang Rui, he’s lying. His alcohol metabolism data shows that he had just finished drinking at the time of the accident. It wasn’t from the night before, like he claimed.”","Fang Rui and Mu Mian took the money to the detention center.","At first, Li Xinyu stubbornly denied everything. But when he saw the bundle of money, his eyes grew moist.","“You have a high alcohol tolerance. Even though the breathalyzer showed you were drunk, you were still fully conscious, weren’t you? You deliberately crashed into them, didn’t you?”","“Of course not! It wasn’t on purpose.”","Fang Rui pointed to the money. “Your mother told me everything. She wants you to confess, reform, and become a better person.”","“I...”","“We also found your debtors. They said you’ve paid off all your debts.”","Li Xinyu remained silent.","“Your alcohol metabolism data shows that you had just been drinking at the time of the accident, not the night before like you said.”","“I confess! I owed over a million in gambling debts. I couldn’t pay it back. Someone approached me, offering to clear my debts and give me another 1.5 million after the job was done. She told me that drunk driving would only get me a few years in prison. I was desperate, so I agreed.”","“Who did she want you to kill?”","“A month ago, she told me to crash into an armored truck and make sure everyone inside died. I was terrified—there were police officers in that truck! But I was so desperate for money that I agreed. Then they suddenly called it off, but they let me keep the money.”","Fang Rui realized the truck must have been the one transporting Chen Shu.","“Later, she came to me again, asking me to kill two people at once—the drivers of a white car and a black car. She told me to make sure they both died in the crash. I had no choice but to stage the accident.”","“What’s her name? Any distinctive features?”","“She’s a young woman in her twenties, quite pretty. But who would’ve thought she’d be so ruthless, even willing to kill police officers.”","Fang Rui had someone sketch a portrait based on Li Xinyu’s description.","When Fang Rui and Mu Mian saw the familiar face, they both thought of the same person."]},{"number":203,"title":"Chapter 203: The Split-Brain Case: The Genius Brain Project","paragraphs":["The person in the portrait actually bore some resemblance to Bai Jing.","The hit-and-run driver, Li Xinyu, provided a detailed account of his meeting with the mastermind behind the incident.","At the time, the girl had arranged to meet him in a desolate area where there were no traffic cameras and very few vehicles passing by, ensuring that no evidence would be left behind.","When the girl met him, she checked his belongings to confirm that he wasn’t recording audio or video before proceeding with the transaction.","As a result, Li Xinyu had no evidence to prove that Bai Jing was the one who had instructed him.","Fang Rui asked, “Did she come alone?”","“Probably, but I’m not entirely sure. She arrived in a car, and it seemed like there was someone else inside.”","“Did you drive to that desolate area alone?”","“Yes.”","“Was there a dashcam installed in the car?”","“I think so. I’m not entirely sure, though. The car was borrowed from a friend, and I didn’t check if it had one.”","“Was your car turned off at the time?” Many people tend to leave their cars running when temporarily parked, which is a bad driving habit. However, if the car isn’t turned off, the dashcam would continue recording.","“No. The car consumes a lot of fuel when starting up, so I thought I’d just grab the money and leave quickly, so I didn’t turn it off. Why?”","“Take me to find that car.”","“Officer, since I’ve confessed and helped you with the investigation, does that count as cooperation? Will you reduce my sentence?”","“That depends on whether you can successfully identify the mastermind.”","Fang Rui had Bai Jing brought in. At the time, Bai Jing had just finished her class. When she saw the police coming for her, she remained calm, said a few words to her classmates, and left the school with the officers.","As soon as Bai Jing entered, Li Xinyu pointed at her and exclaimed excitedly, “Officer, it’s her! This girl gave me a bag of money to bribe me into causing the accident.”","Bai Jing looked at Li Xinyu coldly. “Who are you? I don’t know you.”","“You can’t just deny knowing me now! You forced me to cause the accident. If I didn’t do it, you threatened to have my family killed. You left me no choice but to stage the crash.”","Bai Jing turned to Fang Rui. “Officer Fang, I don’t know him. I don’t understand why he’s framing me.”","“If he doesn’t know you, how could he describe your facial features so accurately?”","“Maybe I just have a common face, or he’s seen me somewhere and decided to frame me.”","“Officer, I’m not lying. If I’m lying, may I die a horrible death!” Li Xinyu swore.","Bai Jing sneered. “Do you have any evidence that I instructed you?”","“I...”","“You have no evidence. This is slander. I’ll hire a lawyer to sue you for defamation.”","Li Xinyu was drenched in sweat. He thought that by identifying the mastermind, he could get his sentence reduced. He didn’t expect this girl to have such strong nerves, refusing to admit anything.","He looked at Fang Rui. “Officer Fang, it really was her. If you interrogate her properly, she’ll confess.”","“Officer Fang doesn’t solve cases that way. The police rely on evidence,” Bai Jing said with a smile, glancing at Fang Rui. “Isn’t that right, Officer Fang?”","Fang Rui replied, “Yes, we solve cases based on evidence. That day, you specifically chose a desolate area to meet Li Xinyu, and he drove there in a car.”","Bai Jing looked at Fang Rui, waiting for him to continue.","“His dashcam was on the entire time, recording your meeting.”","Although the footage from the dashcam wasn’t very clear, it was enough to identify Bai Jing’s face and the moment she handed over the money.","Bai Jing frowned slightly.","Li Xinyu looked at Fang Rui in surprise. So that was why Fang Rui had been looking for the car. He said, “Officer Fang, thank you for proving my innocence. Girl, you can’t deny it now, can you?”","“Miss Bai, when you used Chen Hui to commit murder, you might have escaped legal consequences, but if you keep doing it, evidence will eventually surface.”","Bai Jing shot a venomous glare at Li Xinyu. If looks could kill, he would have been torn to pieces. She thought this fool would be easy to control, but he had turned the tables on her.","Li Xinyu cowered behind Fang Rui. This girl was terrifying.","He stammered, “Don’t look at me like that. I didn’t know the dashcam was on. I didn’t intentionally record evidence. Besides, you’re the one who committed the crime. I didn’t falsely accuse you, so why are you glaring at me?”","Fang Rui declared, “Miss Bai, you’re under arrest.”","In the interrogation room.","Bai Jing sat quietly in her chair, showing no signs of nervousness. She even looked around the room with curiosity.","Fang Rui and Lin Sen sat across from her.","“So this is what an interrogation room looks like. It’s my first time here, but it’s pretty much what I imagined,” Bai Jing said with a smile.","“Bai Jing, do you admit to instructing Li Xinyu to stage the car accident, resulting in the deaths of Director Liu and one of our officers?”","“Don’t you already have evidence? Do you still need my confession? Just lock me up.”","“Why did you kill Director Liu?”","Bai Jing remained silent.","“Why did you kill Zhang?”","“It was a warning. I had already warned you to stop, but you didn’t listen. You had to pay a price.”","“Who is behind your organization?”","Bai Jing continued to stay silent.","“Is it the Jiangmiao Group?”","Still no response.","Lin Sen decided to try a different approach. “Do you know why you were caught?”","Bai Jing’s brow furrowed slightly.","“Given how careful you are, it’s unlikely you’d make such a basic mistake. Why did you personally go to bribe Li Xinyu?”","Bai Jing’s eyes widened. It seemed she had realized that she might have been set up as a pawn.","But she would never betray her organization, and the people behind her knew that well.","Bai Jing said, “It’s fine. Someone has to make sacrifices. I’ll be that person.”","After that, no matter what Fang Rui and the others asked, she refused to speak.","Bai Jing’s phone and computer yielded no useful clues. It was likely she had another phone for contacting her organization.","While they couldn’t get much out of Bai Jing, one thing was clear: she had killed Director Liu to silence him.","Fang Rui and Mu Mian went to Director Liu’s office at Anqi Obstetrics and Gynecology Hospital.","Li had already checked his work computer. According to the system logs, no files had been deleted recently.","Director Liu’s computer contained many files, mostly patient records and medical research papers.","However, two files caught their attention:","“The Genius Brain Project” and “Neuro-Rose: Maternal and Infant Group Test Records.”","Judging by the file sizes, these documents were extensive, spanning at least a hundred pages.","When they opened them, they discovered that the files were encrypted and required a password to access the contents.","“This kind of password is easy to crack,” Li said as he opened “The Genius Brain Project” document. After typing for a while, he hit enter. “Done.”"]},{"number":204,"title":"Chapter 204: The Split-Brain Case: The Second Victim","paragraphs":["The computer screen suddenly flickered, and a pop-up notification indicated that the file had been opened. However, what appeared on the screen was a blank document.","“Oh no, the other party set up a program. If the file isn’t opened with the correct password, the content will be immediately erased,” Li sighed helplessly. “No wonder he didn’t delete the file—it had a self-destruct mechanism.”","Fang Rui asked, “Can the file content be recovered?”","“I’ll try.”","After a while, Li spread his hands and said, “No, it’s completely corrupted.”","They didn’t dare to attempt forcibly opening another file again.","Director Liu’s social media had a lot of contacts, and they needed to go through them one by one. His chat history also needed to be sorted through. However, after a quick glance, they didn’t find any useful leads.","Although they couldn’t see the file’s content, judging by the file name, Director Liu was likely conducting some illegal experiments. This was probably the reason he sought a surrogate mother.","Fang Rui asked Mu Mian, “What is a ‘Neural Rose’? Is that a technical term? Is it some kind of drug or neural tissue?”","Mu Mian replied, “As far as I know, there’s no such technical term as ‘Neural Rose.’ I’ve never come across it before. It’s likely a term they created themselves.”","“What about the ‘Genius Brain Project’? Could it be that they’re trying to use drugs or surgery to make pregnant women give birth to genius babies?” Fang Rui speculated.","If Director Liu was the executor of the Genius Brain Project, then the child in Wang Yuqing’s womb was his experiment. But is it really possible to make someone give birth to a genius baby?","Could it be that Li Yan giving birth to a child with Down syndrome was man-made?","If that were true, their experiment would be downright inhumane.","Mu Mian analyzed, “The Neural Rose is most likely a drug that can make people smarter, but its effects are highly unstable, which is why they keep conducting experiments.”","Fang Rui said, “So the murderer who dumped the body and left a mark on the ground might be guiding us to investigate this matter.”","Li chimed in, “Then why didn’t he just report Director Liu to the police? Why go through all this trouble to guide us? Dumping a body is also a crime, right?”","At that moment, the dispatcher called Fang Rui: “Captain Fang, we just received a report. A child’s body has been found in the wasteland near Star Home...”","Fang Rui and his team immediately drove to the crime scene.","The wasteland was overgrown with weeds, including tall, sharp-bladed silvergrass.","Although it was a desolate area with few visitors, there was a fishpond nearby. The owner of the fishpond discovered the body while feeding the fish and reported it to the police.","A child’s body lay on its side in the grass. The child was about 1.3 meters tall and wore a blue knitted hat.","Mu Mian put on gloves and turned the body over, revealing the child’s tender face.","Mu Mian exclaimed in surprise, “The victim is Yuanyuan?”","After the truth about the death of Star Home’s director was uncovered, Yuanyuan had left Star Home and was sent to a disabled children’s rescue center, where he received treatment and care.","That facility was located in the new district, more than thirty kilometers away from here.","Mu Mian removed his hat. Like the first victim, Yuanyuan’s hair had also been shaved off, and his scalp bore a centipede-like suture line.","Mu Mian said, “The wound on Yuanyuan’s scalp shows no signs of life reaction, just like Victim Tang. His scalp was cut open postmortem. Yuanyuan’s time of death was within the last 12 hours.”","Wang collected several footprints from the ground. One footprint was size 42, and the other was size 41. Based on the size, both footprints likely belonged to men.","The size 41 footprint was quickly confirmed to belong to the person who reported the case.","The other footprint likely belonged to the killer.","“Look here,” Wang said, pulling aside the weeds to reveal a layer of soil where a symbol “დ” was written in blood.","“This crime mark has appeared again. It seems the killer has struck once more.”","Mu Mian placed Yuanyuan’s body into a body bag and took it back for an autopsy.","Fang Rui and Wang went to the facility where Yuanyuan had been adopted to gather more information.","The facility’s director was a middle-aged man with black-framed glasses and a receding hairline. He seemed somewhat impatient.","“Zhang Yuanyuan was a child under our care. He had autism. Half a month ago, he went missing. We’ve been looking for him but couldn’t find him. Officer, do you have any news about him?”","“He went missing, and you didn’t report it to the police?”","“We did report it, but after searching for several days, the police couldn’t find him. Although this child has autism, he’s quite stubborn and often runs off. This isn’t the first time he’s tried to escape. In the past, we’ve always found him, but this time, for some reason, we couldn’t locate him no matter where we looked.”","Wang said in disbelief, “So you just gave up and stopped looking altogether?”","“We searched for over half a month and couldn’t find him. What else could we do?”","Fang Rui asked, “Do you have surveillance cameras here?”","“Yes, there are cameras in the hallways and at the main entrance. We saw Yuanyuan sneak out when the security guard wasn’t paying attention, but we don’t know where he went after that.”","Fang Rui went to the security room to check the surveillance footage, but the facility only kept recordings for half a month. The footage from the day Yuanyuan went missing had already been overwritten.","Wang analyzed, “It’s very likely that the killer abducted Yuanyuan. But he has autism—how could he have been so easily lured away?”","“The person who abducted Yuanyuan was probably someone he knew.”","But as an autistic child, Yuanyuan likely didn’t interact much with anyone outside the children at Star Home.","Fang Rui suddenly thought of Lin Qianyan. He seemed to be friends with Yuanyuan, and Yuanyuan listened to him. But Lin Qianyan was just a child—how could he have orchestrated this?","Mu Mian quickly completed Yuanyuan’s autopsy. Like the first victim, the killer had sawed open Yuanyuan’s skull, severed the corpus callosum connecting the two hemispheres of the brain, and removed half of the brain tissue.","Unlike the last time, this time the killer had taken the right hemisphere.","During the case analysis meeting, she reported the autopsy results: “The external injuries on Yuanyuan’s body show no signs of life reaction, meaning they were inflicted postmortem. There are no typical signs of mechanical asphyxiation or poisoning. It’s preliminarily suspected that Yuanyuan may have died from an illness. However, we’ll need to wait for the pathology report to confirm the exact cause of death.”","Fang Rui asked, “So it’s highly likely that Yuanyuan also died from an illness?”","“Yes.”","“Then what was the killer’s purpose in dumping the body this time?”"]},{"number":205,"title":"Chapter 205: The Case of the Split-Brain Patient: The Meaning of დ","paragraphs":["After work, Fang Rui and Mu Mian drove to the hospital to visit Zhang. Mu Mian had specifically gone to a gift shop to pick out a present and had the store owner wrap it carefully.","Zhang had been moved to the ICU and was still unconscious. The doctors said his condition was very critical, and there was a high likelihood he would remain in a vegetative state. Chen Xue had taken time off and had been sitting outside the ward, waiting for Zhang to wake up.","Mu Mian looked at Zhang through the glass. His head was wrapped in bandages, and he was hooked up to a ventilator, devoid of his usual energy. She shook the gift in her hand and whispered softly to Zhang, \"Officer Zhang, do you want to know what's inside this gift box? You’ll have to get better soon so you can open it.\"","Zhang remained silent and motionless, seemingly unmoved by Mu Mian’s gift. Chen Xue sat quietly on a chair in the hallway. Zhang’s parents had urged her to go home and rest, but she hadn’t left.","Mu Mian comforted her, \"Chen Xue, Zhang will wake up. He still wants to marry you.\"","Chen Xue stared at the ring in her hand and said nothing.","Fang Rui spoke up, \"We’ve caught the person who hit Zhang. The mastermind behind it is Bai Jing, and it’s likely connected to the Jiangmiao Group.\"","Chen Xue continued to look down, seemingly oblivious to Fang Rui’s words, her focus entirely on the ring in her hand.","Fang Rui waited for her to come clean. If she was indeed part of the same organization as Bai Jing, and the organization had harmed Zhang, would Chen Xue betray them for Zhang’s sake?","Mu Mian reached out and hugged Chen Xue, comforting her, \"Chen Xue, Zhang needs you right now. You can’t collapse from exhaustion. You need to rest.\"","\"Alright, I’ll rest tomorrow,\" Chen Xue forced a stiff smile and hugged Mu Mian back.","\"Chen Xue, you have to believe that Zhang will get better.\"","\"Thank you, Mu Mian. No matter what happens, you’ll always be my best friend,\" Chen Xue whispered in her ear.","Mu Mian felt a lump in her throat. She wasn’t sure if Chen Xue was a bad person or if she was deceiving her, but in that moment, she believed that Chen Xue truly saw her as her best friend.","When Mu Mian got home and was eating a sandwich, she thought about the two files again.","The \"Genius Brain Project\"? Was someone trying to create genius babies? Mu Mian remembered her aunt’s words: \"You mustn’t let Miao Miao become smart. Becoming smart will kill her.\" Did her aunt mean becoming a genius?","She glanced at the book on her shelf, *Flowers for Algernon*, a science fiction novel her aunt had given her. In the book, the author described a surgery that could make people smarter. Was her aunt hinting at something?","Mu Mian had read the book before, so when her aunt gave it to her, she hadn’t bothered to open it again. She quickly flipped through it and found a note written in pencil on page 66: \"The Neuro Roseდ can make the brain bloom, but it can also make it wither.\"","How did her aunt know about the Neuro Rose? How did she find out?","Mu Mian grabbed the book and decided to go find Fang Rui.","Shen Xiyin was sitting on the couch in the living room, reading. When she saw Mu Mian rushing out, she asked, \"Mu Mian, where are you going so late?\"","\"Sister, do you know what the Neuro Rose is?\"","Shen Xiyin closed her book and said, \"No, I’ve never heard of it.\"","\"What did our aunt used to do?\"","\"She was a surgeon a long time ago. After that, she stopped working and focused on taking care of her daughter.\"","Mu Mian asked, \"Did our aunt ever research any drugs that could make people smarter?\"","\"I don’t know. I was very young when she left home. Dad never let anyone talk about her, so I don’t know much about her.\"","\"Alright. Sister, I’m going to find Fang Rui.\"","\"It’s late. Isn’t it rude to bother him?\"","\"He’s my boyfriend. It’s fine.\"","\"Then make sure to come back early.\"","Mu Mian ran to knock on Fang Rui’s door.","When the door opened, she excitedly said, \"Fang Rui, I know what that symbol means!\"","But it was Lin Sen who answered the door. Mu Mian frowned, \"Brother-in-law, why are you here? Where’s Fang Rui?\"","\"He’s cooking noodles.\"","Mu Mian looked into the kitchen and saw Fang Rui cooking. So Fang Rui could cook? Why had he been eating instant noodles every day before?","Mu Mian asked, \"Brother-in-law, why are you here eating noodles at Fang Rui’s place?\"","Lin Sen replied, \"Eating noodles is just a bonus. I’m here to discuss the case with Fang Rui.\"","Mu Mian was annoyed, \"Why didn’t you invite me to discuss the case?\"","Just then, Fang Rui brought over a pot of steaming noodles.","Lin Sen pointed at Fang Rui, \"Ask him.\"","\"Fang Rui, why didn’t you invite me to discuss the case? Are you trying to exclude me?\"","\"We were planning to call you over after we finished eating.\"","\"Why didn’t you invite me to eat? I already had a sandwich for dinner, but I could still have some late-night snacks...\" Mu Mian looked at the pot of mushy noodles, \"What is this? Noodles? How did they end up like this?\"","Lin Sen said, \"Now you know why he didn’t invite you to eat.\"","Fang Rui shot Lin Sen a glare.","Mu Mian was baffled, \"Fang Rui, how did you manage to cook noodles into this shape?\"","Fang Rui didn’t answer. What else could it be? The noodles were overcooked.","He got another bowl for Mu Mian and placed it on the table, \"Do you want some?\"","Mu Mian looked disgusted, \"No! Even though my boyfriend made it, I can’t eat noodles that look like this!\"","\"Then I’ll get you some snacks. You don’t eat sweets or junk food, and I don’t have any fruit... Should I make you some instant noodles?\"","\"Forget it, I’ll pass.\"","Lin Sen, however, didn’t seem to mind Fang Rui’s cooking. He served himself a bowl and ate with gusto.","Mu Mian watched him, puzzled, \"Is it really that good?\"","\"I’m just here for the free meal. I don’t have the right to judge,\" Lin Sen handed her an empty bowl, \"Want some? Serve yourself.\"","\"Fine, I’ll force myself to eat a little. It’s my boyfriend’s cooking, so no matter how bad it is, I’ll try it.\"","She had only eaten half of her sandwich earlier, and it had already been digested. Mu Mian was hungry, so she decided to try Fang Rui’s noodles to save face.","To her surprise... it wasn’t bad. It had a strangely satisfying texture.","Mu Mian served herself another bowl.","Lin Sen remarked, \"It tastes good because he used instant noodle seasoning.\"","Fang Rui, holding a freshly made bowl of instant noodles, glared at Lin Sen, \"Then stop eating!\"","After finishing their meal, Mu Mian said, \"I know what that symbol represents. It’s the Neuro Rose. If you look closely, it does resemble a simple drawing of a rose.\"","Fang Rui asked, \"How did you figure that out?\"","Mu Mian held up the book, \"My aunt told me.\"","Fang Rui analyzed, \"Flowers? Could the flowers in this book refer to the Neuro Rose?\"","\"*Flowers for Algernon* is a science fiction novel about a surgery that can make people smarter. The flowers symbolize the surgery. It explores what happens when someone with low intelligence suddenly becomes highly intelligent,\" Lin Sen looked at Fang Rui and sighed, \"You really should read more.\"","Mu Mian protested, \"Fang Rui doesn’t need to read that much. I’ve read a lot of books, so I can explain anything he doesn’t understand!\"","\"...\"","Mu Mian showed them the line her aunt had written: \"The Neuro Roseდ can make the brain bloom, but it can also make it wither.\"","Lin Sen tried to interpret it, \"The blooming probably means the Neuro Rose can bring positive changes to the brain, while the withering refers to its severe side effects.\"","Fang Rui asked, \"How does your aunt know about the Neuro Rose?\"","Mu Mian replied, \"I’m not sure. But my aunt’s daughter was named Miao Miao. She used to be a police officer, but she died of an illness.\"","Suddenly, Mu Mian remembered something and added, \"She was Jiang Yinian’s cousin-in-law. The Jiangmiao Group might have been named after her. My aunt also said that Miao Miao mustn’t become smart, because becoming smart would kill her. I suspect Miao Miao was also a victim.\"","Mu Mian couldn't figure out one thing. According to her aunt, Miao Miao was likely a victim of Neuro-Rose, so why would a company named after Miao Miao continue to research this drug?","Fang Rui said, \"I'll ask the director tomorrow. Since Miao Miao was once a police officer, there must be a file on her in the system.\"","When they mentioned Jiang Yinian's name, Lin Sen exclaimed in surprise, \"Mu Mian, Jiang Yinian was once a suspect in the murder of your parents. At the time, we discovered that the brake lines of your parents' car had been cut, and your father's computer had been stolen. It contained a lot of experimental data and research materials, all of which pointed to Jiang Yinian. However, we didn't have enough evidence to prosecute him back then.\"","Mu Mian was puzzled. \"But my father treated Senior Yinian very well. If he really wanted the data, my father would have given it to him. My father once said that he wanted Senior Yinian to inherit his lab in the future. He had no motive to kill my father.\""]},{"number":206,"title":"Chapter 206: The Split-Brain Case: Yuan Yuan's Friend","paragraphs":["Fang Rui and Lin Sen discovered that the Neural Rose might be related to Mu Mian's father. Jiang Yinian likely stole the research materials from Mu Mian's father and continued the study.","Fang Rui asked, \"Mu Mian, does your sister know what your father's research project was about?\"","Mu Mian shook her head. \"I asked her, but she said she doesn't know. My sister isn't interested in these things; she never liked going to Dad's lab. Whenever Dad tried to explain his papers to us, she would always find excuses to leave because she couldn't understand them.\"","Lin Sen asked, \"Mu Mian, can you still get in touch with anyone from your father's lab?\"","\"No, they've all disappeared. After Dad passed away, they vanished and stopped responding to me. A friend of my sister said it's a case of 'when the person leaves, the tea turns cold.' Since Dad is gone, they no longer need to maintain a good relationship with me.\"","Mu Mian felt a little sad. Those who had been kind to her in the past had mostly done so out of respect for her father or her sister.","Suddenly, Fang Rui thought of a terrifying possibility. If such a drug truly existed and Mu Mian's father was its original developer, could they have also used it on Mu Mian?","It's rare for someone with autism to recover so well—why was Mu Mian the exception?","If the Neural Rose had side effects, what would they be?","Lin Sen also thought of this. He exchanged a glance with Fang Rui, but both of them tacitly chose not to ask the question.","Mu Mian said, \"We can visit my aunt tomorrow morning and see if she can tell us anything. However, her Alzheimer's is quite severe, so I'm not sure if she'll be able to remember anything.\"","The next day, Fang Rui went to Director Wang's office.","\"Director, do you know an officer named Miao Miao?\"","\"There was a Miao Miao. She was my protégé, but she fell ill—a very serious illness. It started with neurological blindness, then her memory began to deteriorate, her bodily functions declined, and eventually, she became vegetative. She passed away not long after. Her boyfriend, Little Jiang, loved her deeply. After her death, he committed suicide.\"","\"Why did she get sick?\"","\"I don't know. She suffered a minor head injury during a mission, but for some reason, her condition worsened drastically. The doctors described her symptoms with one phrase: 'Her brain is collapsing.'\"","\"Director, do you know about the Jiangmiao Group?\"","\"I think it was established by Little Jiang. After Ji Miao's accident, he became a bit unhinged. He even believed in mysticism and tried to hire a master to perform rituals to bring her back to life. What about the Jiangmiao Group? It seems to be involved in a lot of charity work. It's a model enterprise in the city and a major taxpayer.\"","Fang Rui shared this information with Mu Mian and Lin Sen.","They speculated that the Jiangmiao Group's initial research on the Neural Rose was likely aimed at treating Miao Miao. However, after Jiang Yinian took over, the research's purpose shifted, leading to unethical medical experiments.","Lin Sen analyzed, \"It's highly likely that someone within their team betrayed them. They might be guiding us to uncover their experiments and stop them from continuing this research.\"","Fang Rui and Mu Mian drove to the nursing home to visit Mu Mian's aunt, Shen Min, for more information.","The weather had been bad lately, so Shen Min wasn't sunbathing on the lawn as usual. Instead, she was watching TV in her room.","Mu Mian noticed that her aunt seemed to have aged a bit. Her clothes weren't as clean and tidy as before, and there were traces of dried saliva on her collar. The photo album she always carried was also missing.","\"Auntie, do you remember me?\"","Shen Min opened her eyes, glanced at Mu Mian, and then looked away.","\"Auntie, do you remember Miao Miao?\"","Hearing her daughter's name, Shen Min showed no reaction. It seemed she had forgotten everything.","A nurse nearby said, \"Her condition has worsened. She doesn't recognize anyone now. She used to remember her daughter, but now even that memory is gone.\"","Shen Min sat there, dazed and smiling gently. She had forgotten everything, even her daughter, but she seemed to be happier in her own way.","The nurse added, \"Don't worry, Ms. Shen is a VIP client here. She will receive the best care.\"","Fang Rui asked, \"Who arranged for her care?\"","\"Mr. Jiang Yinian. He's also a shareholder in our nursing home, so we make sure to take excellent care of Ms. Shen.\"","After leaving the nursing home, they returned to the police station. Mu Mian saw Lin Qianyan standing at the entrance. As soon as Fang Rui's car approached, he walked over and stopped it.","Fang Rui quickly hit the brakes.","\"Lin Qianyan, what do you want?\"","Lin Qianyan was holding a small whale plushie. He said softly, \"Mu Mian, can I see Yuanyuan?\"","Mu Mian replied, \"Yuanyuan is dead. You can't see him.\"","\"Even his body would be fine.\"","\"Why do you want to see him?\"","\"He has no family or friends. He died, and no one came to see him. He was so pitiful. I once promised him I'd give him a plushie, and now I want to fulfill that promise.\" Lin Qianyan shook the plushie in his hand. \"I've already bought it. It's such a childish thing, and it's useless to me. I just want to give it to him.\"","Mu Mian reached out her hand. \"Give me the plushie. I'll place it next to his body for you.\"","Lin Qianyan refused. \"I don't trust you. I want to give it to him myself.\"","\"Was it you who lured Yuanyuan out of the shelter?\"","\"No.\" Seeing Mu Mian's disbelief, he added, \"Yuanyuan didn't choose to be my friend. He preferred staying in that shelter over living with me. He hated me because I caused the death of his beloved 'Mother Director.'\"","Mu Mian took Lin Qianyan to see Yuanyuan's body.","When Lin Qianyan saw Yuanyuan's pale, frozen body, he didn't show any sadness. Instead, he curiously examined it.","Lin Qianyan asked, \"Mu Mian, you will catch the person who killed him, right?\"","Mu Mian countered, \"Don't you know who the killer is?\"","\"It wasn't my cousin Yinian. I pressed him for answers. It wasn't me either. I don't know who killed him. Why would someone kill an innocent autistic orphan?\"","\"Yuanyuan might have died from an illness,\" Mu Mian said.","Lin Qianyan placed the small whale plushie next to Yuanyuan. \"I promised to give you a plushie, and I've kept my word. I don't know if the heaven you talked about exists, but I hope you've reached it and reunited with your 'Mother Director.'\"","Mu Mian said, \"Lin Qianyan, I think you can choose to be a good person. Stop doing bad things.\"","Lin Qianyan looked at her and said, \"Mu Mian, not everyone is as lucky as you. Goodbye, Mu Mian.\"","Mu Mian watched as Lin Qianyan left.","After leaving the police station, Lin Qianyan got into a car parked by the roadside.","Jiang Yinian glanced at him and asked, \"Lin Qianyan, do you want me to arrange for someone to steal Yuanyuan's body and give it to you?\"","\"Cousin Yinian, I'm not Mu Mian. I don't like cold corpses.\"","\"But he's dead, and I can't bring him back to life. You could try to like it. I can have him preserved as a specimen, so he can stay with you forever in the form of a doll.\"","Lin Qianyan retorted, \"Why don't you turn the person you love into a specimen? Is it because you can't?\"","Jiang Yinian didn't answer.","\"Cousin Yinian, have you found out who killed Yuanyuan?\"","\"Yes. Don't worry, I've come up with a perfect plan to avenge your Yuanyuan.\"","Lin Qianyan corrected him, \"You're not doing this for Yuanyuan. You're doing it for yourself.\"","\"Maybe. I hate being betrayed.\""]},{"number":207,"title":"Chapter 207: The Split-Brain Case: The Dead Killer","paragraphs":["The crime scene where Yuanyuan's body was dumped showed no suspicious traces. After investigating nearby towns, no eyewitnesses were found either. The road near the wasteland had no surveillance cameras installed, making it impossible to trace any leads through video footage.","Fang Rui believed that since the murderer had managed to lure Yuanyuan out of the rescue center, the killer must have known Yuanyuan personally. Given that the killer was likely a doctor, they decided to start by examining Yuanyuan's medical records.","Fang Rui went to the prison to meet Li Min, who had been detained. She was once a staff member at Star Home and knew Yuanyuan well.","Seeing Fang Rui, Li Min seemed uneasy. \"Officer Fang, has something happened?\"","\"Yuanyuan has passed away.\"","Li Min covered her face and began to sob softly. Deep down, she had already sensed that Yuanyuan might not live much longer.","Fang Rui asked, \"Did Yuanyuan ever visit a hospital for treatment? Did he have a doctor he was particularly close to?\"","\"About a year ago, Yuanyuan contracted meningitis, and we sent him to the hospital for two weeks of treatment. The hospital was called Jiangzhou University Second Affiliated Hospital. Yuanyuan got along well with one of the nurses there, but he disliked doctors and was generally wary of strangers.\"","\"What was the nurse's name?\"","\"I think it was Chen Shu, or maybe Lin Shu. I can't remember clearly. Director Zhang was the one who stayed with him during his hospitalization. I was only there for two days.\"","\"Who was Yuanyuan's attending physician?\"","\"It was a doctor surnamed Chen. I think he was the director of their department. I don't remember his full name, but the nurses called him Director Chen.\"","Suddenly, Fang Rui realized why Zhang had said he knew who the killer was. Could it be Director Chen?","Some time ago, Zhang had mentioned that he planned to help Chen Xue reconcile with her father. He had even gone to Director Chen's house to look for him. Could it be that Zhang had noticed something unusual during that visit and recalled a clue when he revisited the hospital, prompting him to call Fang Rui?","Fang Rui and Wang went to Jiangzhou University Second Affiliated Hospital to look for Director Chen.","The receptionist nurse said, \"Didn't I already tell you? Director Chen went out of town to attend an academic conference. He hasn't returned yet.\"","\"It's been so long. Hasn't the conference ended?\"","\"I don't know. Director Chen took two months off, saying he was attending an important conference. We didn't press for details.\"","\"Has he come back at all during this time?\"","\"No, he hasn't been to work at all.\"","Fang Rui then had someone check Director Chen's travel records using his ID number. The results showed that two months ago, Director Chen had taken a flight to Zheng City, and there were no further travel records after that.","Zheng City isn't too far from Jiangzhou City, but driving back would take at least eighteen hours. It was possible that Director Chen had secretly driven back or taken a taxi.","At that moment, Fang Rui received a phone call.","Old Zhang said, \"Captain Fang, didn't you ask us to investigate the sales records of that car model? We found a suspicious person. Someone bought that car at a dealership in a rural area of a neighboring city. He paid with a bag of cash and chose the car very quickly, without even asking about the specifications. We think this person is suspicious.\"","The police had already investigated all car dealerships in Jiangzhou City, thoroughly checking the purchase records of the white car model matching the one owned by Director Liu. However, no suspicious individuals were found. Fang Rui then expanded the investigation to include surrounding cities, online sales channels, and second-hand car markets.","After several days of investigation, they finally found a lead.","Fang Rui asked, \"Does the shop owner know the buyer's identity?\"","\"No, the owner said the buyer didn't say much and didn't reveal any personal information. But based on his accent, the owner thinks he wasn't a local and seemed like an educated person.\"","\"Does the shop have surveillance cameras?\"","\"They do, but the footage has been overwritten by now. It wasn't saved.\"","Fang Rui asked again, \"Does the owner remember what he looked like?\"","\"Captain Fang, hold on, let me ask him.\" Old Zhang spoke to the shop owner over the phone and then said, \"The owner says he remembers. He has a strong impression of that person.\"","\"I'll send you a photo. Ask him if it's this person.\"","\"Okay.\"","Fang Rui sent a photo of Director Chen to Old Zhang, who quickly replied, \"Captain, the owner says it's him. He remembers this person clearly because it's rare for someone to pay with a large bag of cash.\"","Now, the challenge was to find Director Chen's hiding place.","Fang Rui applied for a search warrant and planned to search Director Chen's home first to look for clues.","Director Chen lived in an old neighborhood near Dongjiang Yujing, on the fifth floor.","When they arrived at Director Chen's door, Fang Rui and his team noticed something unusual: the doorknob had no dust on it. Logically, if Director Chen hadn't been home for two months, the doorknob should have been covered in dust.","They rang the doorbell for a long time, but there was no response from inside.","\"We'll have to break in.\"","They forced the lock open, and as soon as the door was pushed open, a strong smell of blood hit them. They stepped inside and saw bloodstains all over the floor. A middle-aged man lay in a pool of blood.","\"The deceased is Director Chen,\" Wang said in shock. \"How did he die?\"","Wang turned his head and saw a bloodied female body lying on the sofa, clutching a blood-stained knife.","Fang Rui put on gloves and pushed the hair away from the female victim's face, revealing a familiar face.","Everyone was stunned. \"Chen Xue? Why is she here? Did Director Chen kill her? But how did Director Chen die too?\"","\"Could it be that Chen Xue found out who the killer was before we did and killed Director Chen to avenge Zhang?\"","Fang Rui said, \"I already told her last night that the mastermind behind Zhang's hit-and-run had been caught.\"","\"Then what's going on here?\"","Mu Mian was notified and quickly arrived at the scene.","Fang Rui comforted her, \"Mu Mian, Chen Xue, she...\"","Mu Mian froze, blinking her eyes, but the scene before her remained unchanged. Chen Xue was covered in blood, lying peacefully on the sofa as if she were asleep.","She remembered Chen Xue's promise from last night. Chen Xue had said she would rest well today.","\"Please keep your voices down. Chen Xue is asleep. She's very tired and needs to rest.\" Mu Mian noticed a blanket on the sofa and picked it up, intending to cover Chen Xue with it.","Fang Rui gently held her hand and said softly, \"Mu Mian, Chen Xue is dead.\"","Mu Mian couldn't hold back her tears. \"Why did she die? Just yesterday, she told me I was her best friend... I have so few friends. Why did she have to die?\"","Fang Rui held her tightly.","\"Fang Rui, I should have understood what Chen Xue meant. She wasn't talking about resting; she knew she was going to die.\" Mu Mian blamed herself. \"Why didn't I stop her in time?\"","The others were also deeply saddened. Chen Xue was their colleague, and her tragic death left everyone heartbroken.","Wang said, \"Mu Mian, we can't let our emotions take over. We need to investigate thoroughly and catch the person responsible for Chen Xue's death. You don't want her to die in vain, do you?\""]},{"number":208,"title":"Chapter 208: The Split-Brain Case: The Truth","paragraphs":["Wang's words had a comforting effect. Mu Mian tried her best to calm herself down.","She had to catch the murderer who killed Chen Xue.","They began to inspect the scene.","The items and furnishings in the living room were relatively tidy, with no signs of a violent struggle. There were three splatters of blood and a trail of bloody footprints in the room, connecting the two bodies.","The bloody footprints were quickly confirmed to belong to Chen Xue, as the size and pattern of the shoe prints matched the shoes she was wearing.","Director Chen had been stabbed twice in the heart, each strike precise and fatal. There were no defensive wounds on his body, and the blood splatters were not chaotic, indicating that Director Chen had not resisted.","Chen Xue had blood splatters on her hair, face, and clothes. She had been stabbed once in the chest, the blade piercing her heart, causing her to quickly die from excessive blood loss.","From the scene, they deduced the sequence of events: Chen Xue suddenly stabbed Director Chen in the heart, and after he fell to the ground, she stabbed him a second time. After Director Chen died, Chen Xue walked over to the sofa and stabbed herself in the heart.","Wang asked in confusion, \"Why did Chen Xue suddenly kill Director Chen? He was her father. Why would she suddenly commit murder?\"","Another person chimed in, \"Could Chen Xue have been hypnotized? Otherwise, why would she suddenly kill someone?\"","Mu Mian carefully examined Chen Xue's body, going over it again and again. She noticed some minor abrasions in Chen Xue's mouth and what appeared to be scratches in her esophagus.","Had Chen Xue been forced to swallow something?","In the autopsy room.","Mu Mian opened Chen Xue's abdominal cavity and removed her stomach. She cut open the stomach and found no food—Chen Xue hadn't eaten for a long time. Inside, Mu Mian discovered a hard object wrapped in plastic.","She picked it up and saw that the plastic film seemed to contain a piece of paper.","Mu Mian first asked Wang to check for fingerprints.","\"No fingerprints,\" Wang reported.","Mu Mian cut open the plastic film and took out the paper inside. It was a handwritten letter, the handwriting messy and hurried.","[To Mu Mian:","Is it you who performed the autopsy on my body? I think it must be. You're so professional; you would calmly examine my body, notice something unusual, and find this letter. I was afraid they would destroy my letter, so I had no choice but to hide it in my stomach.","I'm sorry, I deceived you. I'm not a good person. I was a mole they planted in the police force. They were afraid the police would discover the bodies of the experimental subjects, so they sent me into the City Police Bureau. If such bodies were found, I could alter the autopsy reports to cover up the truth.","The plan was going smoothly at first. I had interned at the City Police Bureau before, and if nothing unexpected happened, I was sure to take over the position of the forensic examiner, Qin. But then, Mu Mian, your arrival disrupted my plans.","So, at first, I didn't like you. You're a genius, and your brilliance was too dazzling, hurting me. At that moment, I realized that all my hard work paled in comparison to the natural talent you were born with.","But to stay, I had no choice but to befriend you. I knew the director would assign an assistant to you, someone who didn't understand social interactions, and as your good friend, I would be the best candidate. Sure enough, I became your assistant.","To avoid raising suspicions, I even pretended to be clueless and joined Zhang in his antics. I acted like a cheerful, outgoing, and somewhat unprofessional forensic examiner, but in reality, I wasn't like that at all. Though perhaps, I had once wished I could be an optimistic and cheerful person.","The first task I received was to stop the police from investigating the missing fetal bodies.","Originally, I didn't even need to intervene, as most people wouldn't care about those children's bodies. But you were different. You even performed DNA tests on those fetuses. You wanted to help them find their mothers. This would expose the secret of their disappearances.","I had to stop you from continuing the investigation. Fortunately, after spending those days with you, I had come to understand you well. I knew you cared deeply about being abandoned by your mother, so I deliberately misled you, stopping you from investigating the children's whereabouts.","The second task I received was to teach you about friendship and love.","I was confused. I didn't understand why they wanted me to do this. But I did it anyway. I deliberately got close to Zhang and made him fall in love with me. He was foolish and quickly fell for me. I deliberately used my relationship with Zhang to show you what love was, constantly guiding you to understand and experience it.","Later, I seemed to understand why they wanted me to do this. You wanted to become a normal person, and to do that, you needed to have emotions. Your sister is an excellent therapist, but she protected you too well, depriving you of the chance to experience complex environments. That's why you were always emotionally dull. I was simply a guide, helping you perceive emotions faster.","I always thought of myself as a rational person, but at some point, I seemed to change. I started to enjoy my current life and even grew to like you as a friend. Your world is so simple; it's enviable.","It's easy to get lost in a role you've been playing for too long. Zhang's mother once said she didn't think I loved her son. I vehemently denied it, and in that moment, I realized I had grown to like Zhang too.","Emotions are uncontrollable. When Zhang's mother tried to stop us from being together, I even thought about quitting my job. But quitting wouldn't just mean leaving my job; it would also mean abandoning my undercover mission. And they wouldn't allow that.","Chen Shu's appearance shattered my peaceful life. Because I received my third task: to kill Chen Shu.","It was a risky move, as I knew I might be exposed. But I had no choice but to accept the mission.","Chen Shu had been exposed. She didn't want to live, nor could she continue to live. So when she entered the interrogation room, she gave me a look, signaling me to kill her.","Do you remember the bag of rat poison you brought back from Lu Tian's house? When we were testing for toxins, I stole a bit of it. I knew then that I would eventually use it. When Wang went in to see Chen Shu, I handed her a cup of water to give to Chen Shu. The water was laced with rat poison.","Chen Shu knew there was poison in it. She would drink the water just before leaving the interrogation room, pretending to sip it during the interrogation to avoid suspicion. Then she would hold it in until the transport vehicle left the police station, where she would let the guards discover she had been poisoned.","After Chen Shu died, I replaced the paper cup in the trash and smeared rat poison solution on her collar. After it dried, I sent her clothes for testing.","It wasn't a perfect plan, and I even suspected you already knew the truth.","The final task I received was to kill my father.","When the child with Down syndrome appeared, I knew there was a traitor among us. I immediately informed them. But I didn't expect Zhang to get injured while tailing Director Liu. It was then that I learned the traitor was my father.","Seeing Zhang lying motionless in bed, my heart turned to ash. I wanted to kill myself, but before that, I had to avenge Zhang.","The organization promised me they would make Bai Jing, who acted without authorization, pay the price. In return, I had to kill someone for them—someone I had long wanted to kill: my father. They kept their promise, and so did I. I finally avenged Zhang.","Mu Mian, if Zhang dies, bury me with him. Choose the most beautiful cemetery for us.","If he survives, tell him I was always lying. I never loved him. The engagement ring is in the drawer of Zhang's hospital room. Please return it to him.","Mu Mian, I'm sorry. I can't betray my organization. I can only tell you this much. Please stop investigating this matter. Let it end here. You can't defeat them.","Mu Mian, don't grieve for me. You will have more friends and a happy life in the future.","Mu Mian, goodbye!]"]},{"number":209,"title":"Chapter 209: The Split-Brain Case: Case Closed","paragraphs":["The police searched Director Chen's house. In his bedroom, Fang Rui noticed a photo frame containing a picture of Director Chen with a young Chen Xue and Chen Xue's mother. The photo and frame appeared old, showing signs of age, yet they were well-preserved.","Inside a drawer, Fang Rui found a photo album filled with numerous group photos, including pictures with patients and their families. On the back of each photo, the names of the patients were written. It seemed Director Chen used this method to document the more unique patients he had encountered.","One particular photo caught Fang Rui's attention—it was a picture of Director Chen and Chen Hui, with a wheelchair-bound woman suffering from cerebral palsy seated between them. On the back of the photo, the name \"Chen Minrong\" was written. Fang Rui had previously investigated Chen Hui's family background and knew that Chen Hui's aunt shared this name. This suggested that Chen Hui's aunt had likely been one of Director Chen's patients.","The drawer also contained several bottles of medication, commonly prescribed for treating depression. The bottles were nearly empty, indicating that Director Chen might have been suffering from severe depression.","In Director Chen's study, the police discovered a toolbox containing surgical instruments: scalpels, hemostats, an electric bone saw, and more. They sprayed luminol reagent on the tools, but there was no fluorescent reaction—no blood was detected.","The police continued their search, spraying luminol on the floors and walls of both the bedroom and study. Again, there was no fluorescent reaction, suggesting no bloodstains were present—this was not the location where the deceased's brain had been dissected.","Next, they inspected the bathroom. After spraying luminol on the tiles and walls, they still found no traces of blood. However, they noticed that the tiles appeared unnaturally white, with their patterns somewhat faded. Upon further testing, they discovered traces of hypochlorite, a bleaching agent that could interfere with the luminol reaction.","Determined, the police examined harder-to-clean areas, such as the gaps between tiles and the corners of the bathroom. Finally, in the crevice where the toilet met the floor tiles, they detected bloodstains and successfully extracted a blood sample. DNA analysis confirmed that the blood belonged to Yuanyuan.","This evidence strongly suggested that the bathroom was the site where the body had been dissected.","The police also located a white car in the parking lot of Director Chen's residential complex. Although the license plate had been changed, the car's make and color matched the one seen in the surveillance footage.","The car's front showed no visible scratches, but upon closer inspection, Wang noticed signs of recent paintwork. No bloodstains were found inside the vehicle, but on the driver's side floor mat, they discovered various types of soil and fragments of green grass.","After analysis, one type of soil matched the soil from the first body disposal site, while the grass fragments were identified as a type of wild grass found in flower beds. This confirmed that the car had been used in the first body disposal case.","The mounting evidence pointed to Director Chen as the perpetrator of both body disposal cases.","On Director Chen's desk in the study, Fang Rui found several crumpled pieces of paper. One of them bore a hastily scribbled note:","\"Neural Rose is a scam. There are no miracles!","They've gone mad. I must stop them!","Xue, I'm sorry, Dad.\"","It seemed Director Chen's mental state had deteriorated. His actions of disposing of bodies and leaving behind symbols might have been an attempt to draw the police's attention and halt the research he opposed.","Fang Rui thought of Chen Hui, who had also suffered a mental breakdown and killed multiple pregnant women. Could Chen Hui's crimes have been motivated by a similar desire to stop the research?","Even the Star Home case seemed to be guiding the investigation toward the Jiangmiao Group.","Was all of this truly a coincidence?","Despite a thorough search of the house, the brain tissue taken by Director Chen was never found.","Fang Rui convened a meeting to conclude the case.","The mood was somber. Although the perpetrator had been identified, the team had lost two colleagues. Zhang remained in critical condition at the hospital, while Chen Xue had killed the perpetrator and then taken her own life.","Lin Sen analyzed, \"In her suicide note, Chen Xue mentioned that Bai Jing had been sent to prison by their organization. Could the dashcam footage have been intentionally recorded for us?\"","Li added, \"It's possible they replaced the dashcam's memory card. When I examined it, I noticed the card wasn't the original, but since the video hadn't been edited, I didn't think much of it. Now it seems they deliberately provided us with evidence.\"","Fang Rui realized that the opposing side had set up a perfect trap: Chen Xue, the disloyal mole, was dead; Director Chen, the betrayer, was dead; and the police had been trying to find a breakthrough through Bai Jing, but she had been imprisoned by her organization—a blatant message that no leads would come from her.","Fang Rui and Lin Sen visited Bai Jing at the detention center.","She had been held for many days but remained in good spirits. Upon seeing Fang Rui and Lin Sen, she smiled and asked, \"Why hasn't Mu Mian come? Are you afraid she'll learn the truth?\"","Fang Rui inquired, \"Was Mu Mian also a subject of Neural Rose?\"","\"I don't know.\"","\"Why did you assign Chen Xue the task of guiding Mu Mian to perceive emotions?\"","\"I know nothing about Mu Mian. Asking me is pointless.\"","Fang Rui pressed, \"The memory card in Li Xinyu's dashcam was replaced. Who do you think did it? Who knew you were there and recorded the scene?\"","Bai Jing frowned. She had suspected she was being discarded, and now she was certain of it.","Bai Jing began to speak, \"My mother was once a beautiful woman. She was wealthy, but her life was full of misfortune. She was deceived by men repeatedly until she met a psychologist. She thought he was her soulmate, but he swindled her out of her money and drove her to madness.\"","\"Do you know how painful it is to live with a madwoman? You can't imagine it because none of you have a mother like that. I couldn't even leave her because I loved her, because she needed me so much.","Then, I met someone who helped me cure my mother. Though she wasn't entirely lucid, she no longer dwelled on her past pain. She became happier, the kind of mother I needed.\"","Fang Rui and Lin Sen understood that Bai Jing would never betray her organization.","\"Perhaps you think what we're doing is evil, but we believe we're creating miracles.\"","Fang Rui retorted, \"Miracles? What about Yuanyuan, who you killed? Was she just a lab rat? How many more Yuanyuans are there?\"","\"Medical progress requires sacrifice. If you look back at medical history, you'll find that every advancement is built on countless lives. These sacrifices are insignificant.\"","Bai Jing refused to reveal more.","After the case was closed, Chen Xue's mother, accompanied by Chen Xue's Aunt and Aunt-in-law, came to claim Chen Xue's body.","Chen Xue's Mother wept softly, blaming herself, \"It's all my fault. I kept telling Xue how her father abandoned us. I repeated it over and over, making her hate her father.\"","Chen Xue's Mother had despised the man who abandoned their family, forbidding Chen Xue from seeing him and constantly reminding her that only her mother loved her, that her father hated her because she wasn't a genius, that he wanted a brilliant child instead.","She thought this would motivate Chen Xue to study harder, and indeed, Chen Xue excelled. But she never imagined that her hatred had warped Chen Xue's psyche, leading her to commit such extreme acts.","Chen Xue's Aunt said, \"It's not your fault. It's her irresponsible father's doing. He deprived Xue of a father, and now he's caused her death. He's a curse!\"","Chen Xue's Mother clung to her daughter's body, crying, \"Xue, he was your father. No matter how terrible he was, you shouldn't have killed him.\"","But Chen Xue could no longer respond. She had become a cold, lifeless corpse.","Fang Rui said, \"Auntie, please accept my condolences and take care of yourself.\"","Chen Xue's Mother still couldn't come to terms with Chen Xue's death. She tightly held onto Chen Xue, crying, \"Xue, don't leave me. How can I go on without you? Please wake up, please...\"","Fearing that Chen Xue's Mother might collapse from grief, Fang Rui gently led her to the restroom.","As he walked, Fang Rui thought of the photo frame. He wondered if Director Chen didn't love Chen Xue after all—perhaps he just cared more about his career.","But Fang Rui decided not to mention the photo frame to Chen Xue's Mother. Some things, even if known, wouldn't change anything."]},{"number":210,"title":"Chapter 210: Rediscovery","paragraphs":["Although Director Chen's case had concluded, they did not stop their investigation into the \"Neural Rose.\"","The next day, Fang Rui received a call from Zhang's Mother: \"Fang Rui, Zhang's condition has improved a lot today. He can speak now.\"","In the past few days, Zhang's condition had already been improving. He had gradually regained the ability to breathe on his own and had been moved out of the ICU. The doctors said there was a high probability he would recover.","Zhang's parents had been afraid of disturbing Fang Rui and the others at work, and even more afraid of raising false hopes, so they hadn't informed them earlier. Only when Zhang was able to sit up today did they finally notify Fang Rui.","\"By the way, Fang Rui, do you know where Chen Xue is? I haven't been able to reach her on the phone. If you can get in touch with her, please let her know.\"","Fang Rui was both happy about Zhang's recovery and saddened by Chen Xue's death. His voice choked as he replied, \"Auntie, Chen Xue... she won't be able to come.\"","\"Why? Is she sick? Then she should rest well. She can come whenever she's ready.\"","\"Yes.\"","Fang Rui didn't tell her the truth.","When their colleagues at the police station heard that Zhang had woken up, they all bought flowers and fruit baskets after work—the largest fruit baskets in the store and the biggest, most beautiful bouquets. They went to the hospital together to visit Zhang.","Mu Mian's eyes were swollen from crying. She said to Fang Rui, \"If Officer Zhang finds out about Chen Xue's death, he'll be heartbroken.\"","\"Let's not tell him for now.\"","\"But he'll find out eventually.\"","In the end, they all decided to keep the news of Chen Xue's passing a secret.","Zhang had now been moved to a general ward. When they entered the room, he was sitting there, staring blankly into space.","Seeing so many people come in, he glanced at them, then looked away and continued to stare blankly.","Their hearts sank. Could Zhang have lost his mental faculties? But they quickly reassured themselves—at least he was alive.","Zhang's parents greeted them warmly as they entered.","\"Officer Zhang, this is a gift for you,\" Mu Mian said, placing a beautifully wrapped present on the bedside table.","Zhang glanced at the gift and asked in a hoarse voice, \"Who is Officer Zhang?\"","Mu Mian replied, \"It's you.\"","\"Am I called Officer Zhang?\"","\"Don't you remember your name?\"","\"No. My mind is completely blank.\"","Everyone turned to Zhang's parents.","Zhang's Mother sighed and explained that Zhang had lost his memory.","After Zhang woke up, the doctors had conducted tests and quickly reached a conclusion: \"This patient is likely suffering from retrograde amnesia. He has forgotten his past. His temporal lobe is damaged, and since the temporal lobe is associated with memory, this injury could lead to memory loss.\"","Retrograde amnesia typically refers to the loss of episodic memories—memories of past events—while procedural memories, such as learned skills, remain intact.","\"Will his memories come back?\" Zhang's Mother asked, her voice trembling.","\"Probably not. If the amnesia were caused by a concussion, there might be a chance, but his is due to brain damage. The likelihood of recovery is low. However, we will arrange for him to receive relevant treatments.\"","\"Will his ability to form new memories be affected?\"","\"It's hard to say at this point. But based on our experience, there will likely be some impact.\"","Mu Mian felt deeply saddened. If Officer Zhang no longer had his past memories, was he still the same Officer Zhang?","Zhang looked at Mu Mian and Fang Rui. They seemed familiar to him. He asked, \"Are you all my good friends? Did I have so many friends before?\"","Everyone replied, \"Yes, we're your good friends and colleagues.\"","Mu Mian introduced herself, \"Hello, Officer Zhang. My name is Mu Mian.\"","Fang Rui said, \"Zhang, I'm Fang Rui.\"","Wang Yu joked, \"I'm Wang Yu. You used to call me 'Little Wang.' You can still call me that.\"","Zhang couldn't help but laugh. \"Your name is 'Little Turtle'? That's such a funny nickname.\"","\"Hey, Zhang Qiang, it's 'Little Wang'! 'Little Wang'! Zhang Qiang, you have to remember me, okay? We're good brothers. You can't forget me again.\"","\"Got it, Little Turtle.\"","\"It's 'Little Wang'! Fine, call me whatever you want. But you have to remember me.\"","\"Okay, I'll remember you, Wang Yu.\"","\"I'm Li Weiyi, the one you always teased for being single. Once you're out of the hospital, we'll play video games together on weekends like before. I promise I won't call you bad at it.\"","One by one, the others introduced themselves. They were reintroducing Zhang to their lives.","Zhang carefully studied each face, trying to commit them to memory so he would recognize them the next time they met. He looked at them over and over, but he felt like someone was missing.","Who was missing?","Zhang asked Li, \"Why was I able to tease you about being single? Did I have a girlfriend? Where is she? Why hasn't she come to see me?\"","Li's eyes reddened, and he quickly covered, \"No, we always teased each other. If you had a girlfriend, would you still be playing video games with me?\"","Zhang asked again, \"So, I'm single too?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"That's so sad.\"","\"Yeah. Me, Little Wang, and you—we're all single and miserable.\"","Zhang pointed at Fang Rui and Mu Mian. \"So, are they a couple?\"","Wang teased, \"Zhang, you're still such a shipper!\"","Zhang looked down at the mark on his ring finger, a circular indentation where a ring might have once been. His head started to ache, and his heart felt hollow, as if a cold wind were blowing through it.","He felt like he had forgotten someone very important, but all his friends and family were here. Who could be missing?","Zhang asked, \"How did I get hurt?\"","\"A car accident.\"","\"Ah, let me guess why. You said I'm a police officer. Did I get into a high-speed chase with a criminal, and then we crashed, which is how I ended up in the hospital?\"","Mu Mian's eyes welled up with tears, but she didn't speak. Even though Officer Zhang had lost his memory, he was still the same goofy, imaginative person he had always been.","Fang Rui said, \"Yes, you're a hero.\"","\"Wow, was I really that amazing?\"","\"Very much so.\"","\"Why are your eyes all red? I'm awake now. Shouldn't you be happy?\"","Mu Mian said, \"We're happy but also sad.\"","\"Hahaha, how can 'happy' describe sadness? Your grammar isn't great.\"","\"I never studied grammar.\"","Zhang looked at the huge bouquet in Fang Rui's hands and laughed. \"You didn't have to bring such a big bouquet! But I guess this means you're my best friend.\"","\"Yes.\"","Mu Mian added, \"I'm also a very good friend of yours.\"","\"I can tell. You're the one crying the most. Your eyes are all swollen. I must be your best friend.\"","\"Yes.\"","Since Zhang had just recovered, they couldn't stay too long and disturb his rest. After chatting with him for a while, they left the hospital.","Outside the hospital gate, Wang and Li crouched by the roadside, silently crying.","Zhang had lost his memory. He had forgotten everything, but he was still the same Zhang they had always known—their dear colleague, forever."]},{"number":211,"title":"Chapter 211: Neural Rose: Cognitive Test","paragraphs":["On the surface, Jiangmiao Group appeared to have no issues, and Fang Rui and his team had no direct grounds to initiate an investigation. The bureau chief collaborated with the tax bureau, using a tax audit as a pretext to scrutinize all of Jiangmiao Group's operations.","The primary revenue of Jiangmiao Group came from its private hospitals and high-end rehabilitation centers, followed by the distribution of various medical equipment, and lastly, the patent fees from its pharmaceutical company. That pharmaceutical company had been operating at a loss for a long time, but Jiang Yinian continued to invest heavily in it. Over the past two years, it had gradually started turning a profit.","They also discovered that Jiangmiao Group had made donations to numerous university medical laboratories. Recently, they had donated a significant sum to the psychology department of Jiangzhou University to fund a research project on adolescent cognitive abilities.","Fang Rui and Lin Sen meticulously reviewed all of Jiangmiao Group's business ventures. The psychology department's project at Jiangzhou University caught Lin Sen's attention. He wondered, \"Why would Jiangmiao Group fund a project like 'The Investigation into Adolescent Cognitive Abilities in Jiangzhou City'?\"","Fang Rui asked, \"Cognitive abilities? How do you even study that? Do they scan brains or something?\"","\"Human cognitive abilities encompass many aspects—memory, attention, sensation, perception, and so on. Each of these has specific experimental paradigms for testing. For example, the cancellation test can be used to assess attention,\" Lin Sen explained.","\"What's the purpose of such a study?\" Fang Rui pressed.","Lin Sen replied, \"On one hand, it helps to understand the cognitive ability levels of adolescents in Jiangzhou City, providing data to support the implementation of educational policies. On the other hand, it establishes normative data for cognitive tests, which is useful for future research.\" He couldn't help but add, \"But honestly, it doesn't have much scientific significance.\"","Mu Mian chimed in, \"Exactly. Because this data won't be recognized internationally, it can't be published in academic papers. It's like many psychological assessment scales—even if someone in China develops new norms, people still rely on norms established decades ago abroad. That's why I often question the rigor of psychological assessments.\"","\"...\" Fang Rui was a bit lost.","Lin Sen thought for a moment and said, \"Actually, this is also a large-scale screening test. It can identify students with different levels of cognitive abilities.\"","Fang Rui speculated, \"Could Jiang Yinian be trying to select experimental subjects who meet his criteria?\"","They all fell silent.","Mu Mian analyzed, \"The experimental subjects we previously investigated—autism patients, stroke patients, and infants with Down syndrome—all had brain abnormalities. Could his next step be to use normal individuals as subjects?\"","Fang Rui recalled what Director Chen had written on the paper: They've gone mad!","Fang Rui reasoned, \"Could this be why Director Chen defected? If they were only experimenting on patients with pre-existing brain conditions, it wouldn't be as cruel. After all, trying new drugs is also a form of treatment, even if the risks are higher. It still offers them a chance at recovery. But if they're conducting illegal drug experiments on normal individuals, that would completely cross the line of ethical and moral boundaries.\"","Lin Sen added, \"Their 'Genius Brain Project'—could it be about selecting students with poor cognitive abilities and turning them into geniuses through drugs? There are quite a few pharmaceutical companies abroad that have researched so-called 'smart drugs,' but those only temporarily increase cortical activity and come with significant side effects. The drugs Jiang Yinian is researching are likely even more immature and carry greater risks.\"","Mu Mian sighed, \"Jiang Yinian has changed. How could he believe he can create geniuses? Education and drugs can promote intellectual growth, but they can only create talent, not genius. Genius is determined by genes.\"","Lin Sen said, \"Xiyin mentioned to me a couple of days ago that the psychology department's project at Jiangzhou University is wrapping up. They've already collected all the data and are in the processing phase. That means Jiang Yinian has likely already obtained all the test results.\"","Fang Rui suddenly thought of Bai Jing and said, \"No wonder Bai Jing suddenly went back to graduate school. Could her mission be to steal this research data?\"","Lin Sen replied, \"Possibly. But getting his hands on this data would be incredibly easy for him. The testing was done using a cognitive assessment system, and all the data is aggregated in the backend with cloud backups. The company that developed the system definitely has all the data, and that company is also under Jiangmiao Group.\"","Lin Sen recalled hearing about the project from Shen Xiyin. He remembered the name of the company that developed the assessment system—it matched one of the companies listed in the business documents he had just reviewed.","Mu Mian said, \"The faculty in the psychology department at Jiangzhou University were all assigned tasks. My sister has been busy with this recently. She might have access to all the data.\"","When Mu Mian returned home from work, she noticed that Shen Xiyin had come back early.","\"Sister, are you done with work?\"","Shen Xiyin was cooking and replied, \"Yes, the tasks assigned by the department are finished.\"","\"Sister, do you have all the data from that research project?\"","Shen Xiyin paused while chopping vegetables and asked, \"Why the sudden interest in this?\"","\"We're investigating a case, and I think it might be related to this.\"","\"The testing system only gave me partial access. I can only see the data for the school I was responsible for. Mian, I'm sorry, but this test was conducted with real names, so I can't just show you the data. It involves the privacy of many students.\"","Mu Mian insisted, \"Sister, this case is important. Jiang Yinian might be using this test to screen for the experimental subjects he wants. We have to stop him.\"","Shen Xiyin frowned, \"What is he trying to do?\"","\"We don't know for sure. He seems to have a plan called the 'Genius Brain Project.' We suspect he wants to create geniuses through neural manipulation.\"","Shen Xiyin scoffed, \"He's truly insane.\"","\"Why has Jiang Yinian become like this?\"","Shen Xiyin said, \"Mian, I can give you all the data. The department head isn't very familiar with the system, so he gave me his account, which has full access to all the data.\"","Shen Xiyin helped Mu Mian log into the system. \"You can directly screen for the student list you need within the system.\"","\"Thank you, sister.\"","Mu Mian took her laptop to Fang Rui's place. Lin Sen was also there.","They briefly reviewed the students' scores across various indicators. The differences weren't too significant.","Mu Mian said, \"We have the data, but what criteria would he use to select his targets?\"","Lin Sen suggested, \"Let's start by screening out the extreme values and investigate those students first. Maybe we'll find some leads.\"","\"Okay.\"","Soon, they had a list of students with the lowest cognitive ability levels."]},{"number":212,"title":"Chapter 212: Neural Rose: The Laboratory","paragraphs":["The next day, Fang Rui sent teams to visit the parents of the students on the list, asking if they had recently given their children any medication. At the same time, they reminded the parents not to believe in the existence of any so-called \"smart pills.\"","To be on the safe side, Fang Rui also reported the situation to Director Wang.","The director pondered for a moment and said, \"Fang Rui, all of this is just speculation at this point. We have no evidence, and no case has been filed. Under these circumstances, it's impossible to apply for a search warrant.\"","\"Director, what if he really is using those students to test drugs? That could lead to a major medical accident! The situation is critical, and we must stop him immediately! If you don't agree, I'll investigate on my own!\" Seeing that the director remained unmoved, Fang Rui decided to leave and find another way.","\"Come back! Can't you let me finish? You want to investigate his lab, right? I'll contact the fire department later. We can use a fire safety inspection as a pretext to have the firefighters accompany you for a surprise inspection. That way, it'll be legal.\"","\"Director, why didn't you just get to the point earlier?\"","\"I *was* getting to the point! You can't just rush into things; you need to strategize.\" Director Wang waved his hand. \"Go ahead and investigate.\"","Captain Chen from the fire department knew Fang Rui and provided them with a few sets of firefighter uniforms.","He glanced at Mu Mian and asked, \"Is this young lady coming too?\"","\"Don’t you have a uniform that fits her?\"","\"No, but it’s fine. She can just wear her own clothes. If anyone questions it, I’ll say she’s a clerk, handling paperwork. Being a bit shorter won’t matter.\"","Mu Mian retorted, \"I’m not short. I’m 158 cm, only 1.5 cm below the average height for women in Jiangzhou City. If I wear slightly higher heels, I’ll reach the average height.\"","\"...\"","Jiang Yinian’s private lab was located at Colenda Pharmaceuticals, a subsidiary of the Jiangmiao Group. The company was divided into a pharmaceutical factory and a research center. The research center was a four-story building with a futuristic design.","Manager Liu, the head of the research center, came to greet them. \"Didn’t we just have a fire inspection last month?\"","Captain Chen replied, \"This is a follow-up inspection. Last week, a lab at a university in the country caught fire, nearly causing casualties. So, the higher-ups have ordered us to conduct stricter inspections of labs in the city. Don’t worry, this time it’s just about rectifying issues. No fines—yet. But if things aren’t fixed by the next inspection, there will be penalties.\"","\"I haven’t heard about that incident,\" Manager Liu said, his gaze lingering on Mu Mian.","\"There are so many news stories nationwide; you can’t possibly know them all.\"","\"Alright. Just make it quick, so you don’t disrupt our work.\"","Once inside the building, they headed straight to the fourth floor, where Jiang Yinian’s private lab was located.","The lab was spacious, divided into multiple sections by glass partitions, making the entire space visible from the entrance.","There were over a dozen employees working inside, all of them young.","As she entered the lab, Mu Mian was stunned. The lab was almost identical to her father’s. The placement of every instrument, the orientation of the windows—everything was replicated exactly.","\"What’s wrong?\" Fang Rui whispered.","\"He copied my father’s lab.\"","Captain Chen and his team conducted a thorough inspection of the lab’s fire safety equipment. To make it look convincing, he occasionally raised questions: \"Has this fire extinguisher been inspected regularly? Really? Don’t lie to me. If it’s been inspected, where’s the inspection record?\"","Fang Rui and Mu Mian carefully searched the lab but found nothing suspicious. All the experimental procedures appeared to be standard.","During the search, Mu Mian noticed a lot of information. Based on the file names on the desks, they were conducting research on drugs for Alzheimer’s disease. Although she couldn’t see the full reports, Mu Mian suspected that Jiang Yinian was replicating the research her father had been working on before his death.","The inspection went smoothly, but when they tried to inspect one of the offices, Manager Liu stopped them. \"I’m sorry, but this is our boss’s office. It’s off-limits to anyone without his permission.\"","\"But we need to check for fire hazards.\"","\"Well...\"","\"Let them in.\"","Jiang Yinian’s voice came from behind them.","Mu Mian and Fang Rui turned around, meeting his gaze.","Jiang Yinian looked at Mu Mian and Fang Rui. \"Mu Mian, Officer Fang, if you wanted to visit my lab, you could have just asked me. I’d be happy to give you a tour.\"","Manager Liu looked surprised. \"You’re police officers?\"","\"Manager Liu, go back to your work. I’ll handle this personally.\"","Jiang Yinian said to Mu Mian, \"You wanted to search my office, right? Go ahead.\"","Mu Mian and Fang Rui entered Jiang Yinian’s office. Mu Mian noticed that his office was also an exact replica of her father’s.","Mu Mian couldn’t understand. If he had caused her father’s death, why would he replicate his lab? Was it some kind of tribute?","After Mu Mian and Fang Rui entered the office, Jiang Yinian closed the door behind them, shutting everyone else out.","The walls of the office were made of one-way glass, allowing those inside to see out, but not the other way around.","Mu Mian couldn’t hold back any longer. \"Senior Jiang, why did you cause the car accident that killed my parents? My father liked you so much. Why would you do that to him?\"","Jiang Yinian replied, \"Mu Mian, it wasn’t me. Will you believe me?\"","\"No. I’ve learned to recognize lies now. I think you’re lying again.\"","Jiang Yinian looked hurt. \"No one believes me. But it’s fine. I’m continuing his research as a way to honor him.\"","Mu Mian asked, \"Are you talking about Neuro-Rose?\"","\"I’m referring to Professor Shen’s final research project—the one on Alzheimer’s drugs.\" Jiang Yinian glanced at the people outside. \"I’ve gathered many people to continue that research.\"","\"But it’s already been proven wrong.\"","\"So what?\"","\"They’re all wasting their talents. You’re misusing their abilities,\" Mu Mian couldn’t help but point out.","\"I don’t need them to produce results for me. But they’re not losing anything either; they’re getting paid well. Do you think they’re passionate about research? If they were, they would have left by now.\"","Mu Mian realized she couldn’t understand Jiang Yinian’s mindset at all.","She pressed on, \"What exactly is your Genius Brain Project?\"","\"Mu Mian, don’t you think the root of inequality among people lies in the inequality of intelligence? Intelligence determines ability, which in turn affects social status and income. If we could eliminate the gap in intelligence, wouldn’t the world be a fairer place?\"","Fang Rui couldn’t comprehend why Jiang Yinian would hold such an extreme view. He himself was a genius, a beneficiary of this so-called inequality. Why would he want to dismantle it?","Mu Mian corrected him, \"Senior Jiang, you can’t achieve that.\"","Jiang Yinian smiled. \"I was just joking earlier. What Genius Brain Project? It sounds childish. Mu Mian, if you’re interested in our research, feel free to look through the reports on the desk.\"","Mu Mian didn’t hold back and openly examined the reports on the desk. But after flipping through them, she realized there was no trace of Neuro-Rose here.","This lab wasn’t being used for experiments at all. It was just a place for Jiang Yinian to reminisce. He had gathered groups of people to repeat her father’s research, only to fail again and again."]},{"number":213,"title":"Chapter 213: Neural Rose: Experimental Subject","paragraphs":["With Jiang Yinian's permission, they thoroughly searched the laboratory but found no clues, ultimately returning empty-handed.","Captain Chen from the fire department, however, had a fruitful visit. He compiled a full page of issues that needed rectification and patiently explained to Manager Liu how to make the necessary improvements.","\"Did you remember all the issues I mentioned? A small leak can sink a great ship. Fire safety is no trivial matter; it can't be taken lightly. Keep this rectification notice safe. We'll be back for a follow-up inspection,\" Captain Chen said.","Manager Liu smiled as he took the notice. \"No problem, we'll make the changes,\" he replied, though inwardly he couldn't help but grumble, *What are you really here for? Do you even know? Why put on such a convincing act?*","Back at the station, Mu Mian remarked, \"Jiang Yinian must have another lab.\"","\"Where could that other lab be?\" someone asked.","Lin Sen analyzed, \"Labs require a lot of space. If he's conducting illegal experiments, he'd need high levels of secrecy and security. He wouldn't rent a space for it, so the lab is likely built on property he owns or trusts.\"","Fang Rui added, \"Then I'll have someone look into the properties under his name.\"","Lin Sen continued, \"We should also investigate the properties owned by the Lin family.\"","A few days later, the investigation into the students' parents finally yielded some leads.","Old Zhang reported, \"Captain Fang, we've found some clues. One parent mentioned that someone approached her, offering a large sum of money in exchange for her son's participation in testing a new drug. She refused, fearing it might harm her child.\"","Fang Rui and Mu Mian went to visit the parent.","Her name was Li Yushan, a single mother with limited education who made a living running a small food stall. Fang Rui and Mu Mian approached her stall.","It was the weekend, and her son, Linlin, wasn't in school. He sat on a small stool by the roadside, diligently working on his homework.","Fang Rui first supported her business by buying a pile of her fried skewers, planning to share them with the team later. Then he began asking questions: \"Was there someone who approached you, wanting your son to test a drug for them?\"","Li Yushan, busy frying chicken cutlets and strips, replied, \"Are you the police? Your colleagues already came by, and I told them everything.\"","\"Yes,\" Fang Rui confirmed.","\"A few days ago, two people came to me. They said they had developed a drug that could enhance intelligence but needed clinical trials. They chose my son as a test subject. They offered me 200,000 yuan if I agreed. I was furious and chased them away. Hmph, my son is already so smart—why would he need an intelligence boost?\"","Linlin, however, wasn't particularly bright. He often ranked last in his class, struggled with homework, and was frequently called in for parent-teacher meetings. Despite this, Li Yushan believed her son was the best—just not great at exams, but otherwise well-behaved.","\"Do you have their contact information?\" Fang Rui asked.","\"Yes, they gave me a business card, saying I could reach out if I changed my mind,\" Li Yushan replied, removing her gloves and pulling a card from her cash box. She handed it to Fang Rui.","The card read: \"Clinical Trial Recruitment Platform\" and listed the recruiter's name as Ye Yuanqing. It was a legitimate third-party company.","Mu Mian crouched beside Linlin, curious about his homework.","She had never seen a child write so slowly. He was meticulous, writing each stroke carefully, but the characters were messy, crooked, and often incorrect.","\"'Gan' is written wrong here. You're missing a stroke,\" Mu Mian couldn't help but correct him.","Linlin added a stroke to the character.","Mu Mian noticed something was off. She examined Linlin's homework and realized he frequently made mistakes—missing strokes, flipping characters, or writing them crookedly.","She pulled out Linlin's cognitive test results and quickly spotted the anomaly.","The memory test had two sections: short-term and long-term memory. The short-term test used numbers, and Linlin scored highly. But in the long-term memory test, which used words, he scored zero.","\"Linlin, can you not read these characters?\" Mu Mian suspected Linlin had dyslexia. It wasn't that he wasn't trying—he simply couldn't write the characters correctly.","Linlin shook his head. \"I can read them,\" he said.","\"Then why can't you write them correctly?\"","Linlin lowered his head and stayed silent.","\"Linlin, it's okay if you can't read them. Just tell me the truth, okay?\"","\"Wah... Mom works so hard to pay for my schooling. I can't not know these characters. I want to study hard so Mom doesn't have to struggle, but I just can't learn. I'm stupid! The characters are like bugs—they keep moving around, and I can't understand or remember them.\"","Hearing her son cry, Li Yushan rushed over and hugged him. \"Linlin, what's wrong? What happened?\"","\"Mom, I'm not stupid!\"","\"Linlin, of course you're not stupid. You're the best, Mom's pride and joy,\" Li Yushan said, shooting a glare at Mu Mian.","\"But I always come last in class. I can't write the characters right!\"","\"You'll get better when you're older.\"","Mu Mian, feeling guilty for upsetting the child, said to Fang Rui, \"I didn't mean to.\"","\"Let's buy him some snacks to cheer him up.\"","\"Okay.\"","Mu Mian went to the supermarket across the street and bought a pile of candies and cookies. On the way back, she dragged Fang Rui into a bookstore.","\"Fang Rui, Linlin might have dyslexia. He struggles to read text. I want to give him some picture books so he can enjoy fairy tales too. All kids love fairy tales,\" Mu Mian said.","\"Good idea.\"","Mu Mian gave the snacks and books to Linlin.","Li Yushan quickly said, \"How much do I owe you? I'll transfer the money.\"","\"This is a gift for Linlin,\" Mu Mian replied, handing the book to Linlin. \"This is a fairy tale. Can you understand it?\"","Linlin flipped through the picture book, fascinated by the illustrations. It was his first time owning a fairy tale book and the first time he could understand one.","\"Thank you, sister.\"","Before leaving, Mu Mian took Li Yushan aside while Linlin was picking wildflowers by the roadside. \"Linlin might have dyslexia. It makes it hard for him to read and write. You might need to send him to a special school.\"","Li Yushan was stunned. \"Are you saying Linlin is really... slow?\"","\"Linlin isn't slow. It's a condition. You should take him to a specialist and follow their advice.\"","\"Okay, thank you.\" But Li Yushan couldn't afford to send Linlin for treatment. She didn't have the money to cover the high costs.","\"Sister, this is for you,\" Linlin said, handing Mu Mian a bunch of wildflowers.","\"Thank you.\"","As they left the food stall, Mu Mian asked, \"Linlin's mom loves him so much. How could she not realize he has dyslexia? Isn't that common knowledge?\"","Fang Rui replied, \"Mu Mian, many mothers don't know about these conditions. They just think their child isn't smart enough.\"","After they left, Li Yushan watched Linlin, who was now engrossed in the picture book. She took out her phone and made a call."]},{"number":214,"title":"Chapter 214: Neural Rose: Kidnapping","paragraphs":["Through their investigation, Fang Rui and his team discovered that most of the parents they contacted were from single-parent families or impoverished households. Their financial situations were poor, and their children's academic performance was subpar, so when they heard about this project, they immediately agreed.","Fang Rui brought Ye Yuanqing, the recruiter from the drug trial platform, into the interrogation room.","Ye Yuanqing had neat short hair. Although she was visibly nervous after being suddenly brought to the police station, she spoke in a composed and logical manner.","\"Officer, our drug trial project is completely legal. This new drug has already passed animal testing and has been filed with the drug regulatory authorities. The entire process is compliant and lawful.\"","\"Do you have the relevant documents?\"","\"Yes. I'll have my colleague send them over shortly.\"","\"Who is the client for this drug?\"","\"The company we signed the contract with is Colenda Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd.\"","This was Jiang Yinian's pharmaceutical company.","Fang Rui asked, \"Can you provide some samples of the drug?\"","\"Of course.\"","\"How do you find test subjects?\"","\"The client has already provided us with a list. We just need to contact them.\"","Ye Yuanqing provided the animal testing report, inspection report, and clinical trial application report for the drug. It was indeed filed with the drug regulatory authorities.","Fang Rui also asked her to provide the signed contracts. Seeing Li Yushan's name on the list, Fang Rui was somewhat surprised.","The police tested the drug, and its components were found to be unproblematic.","Lin Sen analyzed, \"It's also possible that this drug is just a front. During the testing process, they might give the children the actual target drug.\"","Fang Rui realized how cunning Jiangmiao Group was. The contracts had many hidden clauses, and once the parents signed them, even if issues arose later, the company wouldn't be held legally responsible.","About a dozen parents had already signed contracts with the drug trial platform. The police who went to investigate tried to persuade them, but most were lured by the substantial trial fees and refused to terminate the contracts. A couple wanted to back out but were scared off by the hefty breach fees.","Although they had discovered that Jiang Yinian had commissioned a third-party platform to conduct drug trials on the students, the trial project was compliant and the drug itself was unproblematic. This lead had reached a dead end.","Jiang Yinian didn't own many properties, but Lin Qianyan had numerous properties under his name. The police investigated these properties through various means but found no trace of Jiang Yinian's laboratory.","Fang Rui analyzed, \"Jiang Yinian's laboratory must be located in a sparsely populated, independent space. Villa areas and standalone low-rise buildings in the suburbs fit the criteria. But we can't possibly search every villa and low-rise building. It would be inefficient and difficult to investigate.\"","Lin Sen added, \"The founder of Jiangmiao Group is Jiang Yinian's cousin. Could there be villas under his name that haven't been transferred? Maybe the laboratory was set up by his cousin.\"","\"That makes sense. I'll have someone check if his cousin owns any properties.\"","Fang Rui thought for a moment and asked, \"Do drug laboratories consume a lot of electricity and water?\"","\"Laboratories usually have many instruments, so they consume a significant amount of electricity.\"","Fang Rui went to the police chief and asked for his help in collaborating with the power bureau. They wanted the electricity usage data for Jiangzhou City over the past two years to identify any buildings with abnormal power consumption.","After investigating, they found that Jiang Yinian's cousin didn't own any properties.","The power bureau staff sent them several large data files. Just receiving the files took a considerable amount of time.","Wang, watching the download progress bar, couldn't help but say to Li, \"With so much data, it'll take forever to find anything!\"","Li rolled his eyes, \"Are you doubting my skills?\" He turned to Fang Rui and asked, \"Boss, should we skip industrial electricity for now and focus on residential usage?\"","\"Agreed.\"","Li wrote a program to calculate the average electricity consumption per community or village, then filtered out users with abnormally high usage, generating a list.","The filtered results were extensive.","\"Let's remove those in densely populated urban areas.\"","The list shrank significantly.","\"Let's start with the villa areas.\"","While browsing the list, Fang Rui noticed Ye Zeming's villa area. It suddenly occurred to him that Ye Zeming's villa area had strong privacy measures. Apart from surveillance cameras at the entrance, there were no public cameras inside.","\"Shen Min? Is that my aunt?\" Mu Mian noticed that the owner of one villa on the list was Shen Min.","This villa had high and stable electricity consumption.","Fang Rui immediately took a team to the villa area.","\"I want to come too!\" Mu Mian said.","Fang Rui placed a hand on Mu Mian's shoulder and spoke earnestly, \"Mu Mian, stay here. I'm worried this operation might be dangerous.\"","Mu Mian replied, \"Aren't you afraid I might get kidnapped? I think I'm safer with you. You'll protect me, won't you?\"","After some thought, Fang Rui decided to bring Mu Mian along.","The villa area had been developed recently. The design was beautiful, but the occupancy rate was low. The developers had expected the area to become part of the new urban district, so they hastily built high-end villas. However, rumors about the urban development turned out to be false, and the city's expansion bypassed the area, leaving the villas unsold even after significant price reductions.","Fang Rui and his team drove to Shen Min's villa.","Several smart cameras were installed at the entrance. As soon as they approached, the cameras locked onto them and stopped moving.","Fang Rui rang the doorbell, but there was no response.","He rang it again.","This time, footsteps were heard, and the door opened.","A young man with messy hair, wearing glasses and a white lab coat, appeared. He looked nervous.","\"Who are you looking for?\"","\"Do you know Jiang Yinian?\"","\"What do you want?\"","Fang Rui said, \"We've received a report about illegal electrical modifications. We need to inspect the premises.\"","\"That's nonsense. Someone must have made a false report,\" the young man blocked the doorway. \"This is private property. If you barge in, we'll sue you for trespassing!\"","Wang had a quick idea and shouted, \"Does anyone smell something burning? It smells like something's on fire. Quick, everyone, let's go in and put it out!\"","\"On fire? Impossible!\"","Wang pushed past him, \"Hurry, everyone, let's go in! The burning smell is really strong!\"","Everyone entered the villa.","Shen Xiyin had just seen off a visitor and was about to drink some water when her phone rang.","\"Xiyin, it's me!\"","Hearing the familiar voice, Shen Xiyin's expression turned to one of disgust. \"What do you want?\"","\"Xiyin, I'm upset. Mu Mian is being very disobedient. She actually brought the police to arrest me.\"","Shen Xiyin's face paled. \"What have you done to Mu Mian?\"","\"Her safety depends on your decision. There's a car waiting for you downstairs. If you want Mu Mian to be safe, get in the car.\"","\"Jiang Yinian, let me hear Mu Mian's voice. I need to know she's safe.\"","\"Xiyin, if you don't believe me, you can call Mu Mian and Fang Rui to confirm. But don't call the police or speak to anyone else, or I can't guarantee Mu Mian's safety. You're already under my surveillance.\"","\"Jiang Yinian, let me hear Mu Mian's voice.\"","Beep. Jiang Yinian hung up.","Shen Xiyin immediately called Mu Mian.","\"Sorry, the number you dialed cannot be reached.\"","She then called Fang Rui.","\"Sorry, the number you dialed cannot be reached.\"","Shen Xiyin was instantly overwhelmed with fear. Jiang Yinian was a madman. Although he had promised her he wouldn't hurt Mu Mian, the words of a madman couldn't be trusted. Now even Fang Rui seemed to be in trouble.","Jiang Yinian was likely planning to escape with her and Mu Mian, and the best escape route would be by water. Jiangzhou City's foreign trade was prosperous, with many cargo ships heading abroad. Those ships would be the best means for an illegal escape.","Shen Xiyin hurriedly left her office, accidentally knocking over a painting hanging on the wall.","\"Xiyin, what's wrong? Why are you in such a rush?\"","Shen Xiyin didn't answer. She couldn't answer. She couldn't let anything happen to Mu Mian."]},{"number":215,"title":"Chapter 215: Neural Rose: The Capture","paragraphs":["Upon entering the villa, Fang Rui and the others were greeted by a lavishly decorated laboratory, strikingly similar to the one they had seen at the pharmaceutical company. Inside, a few young staff members were handling reagents. When they noticed the intrusion, they paused their work and turned their gazes toward Fang Rui and his team.","The young man who had opened the door spoke up, \"See? There's no fire here. You need to leave! You're trespassing on private property!\"","Fang Rui cut him off, \"Has this laboratory been officially registered?\"","\"I... I don't know. I just started working here,\" the young man stammered.","Fang Rui turned to the others, \"Who's in charge here?\"","The staff members exchanged uneasy glances and shook their heads. \"We're all new here, just started a few days ago. The person in charge isn't here—he stepped out.\"","\"Who is the person in charge?\"","\"We don't know.\"","Wang couldn't contain his frustration, \"You don't know anything, yet you took the job? Aren't you worried about being scammed?\"","\"We just graduated with master's degrees and couldn't find good jobs. Then, suddenly, this high-paying position with great benefits came along, so we applied. At first, we thought the location was odd, but the work seemed normal, so we didn't think too much about it.\"","\"...\"","The room was also equipped with numerous cameras, their lenses like cold, unblinking eyes, watching their every move.","Wang speculated, \"Jiang Yinian must have known we were coming to investigate. He probably hired a bunch of students to work here as a cover. It's likely all the evidence has already been moved. He might even be planning to flee!\"","Fang Rui said, \"I've already sent two people to keep an eye on him. Call in a few more to join them. Once we find evidence here, we'll arrest him immediately.\" A sense of foreboding washed over Fang Rui. Would everything really go as smoothly as they hoped?","\"Got it. I'll make the call now,\" Wang said, pulling out his phone. However, he found there was no signal. \"Boss, the signal here is weak. I'll step outside to make the call.\"","Fang Rui and his team thoroughly searched the first floor of the laboratory. Just like before, they found nothing suspicious.","The second floor served as both living quarters and office space. In one of the offices, they discovered stacks of experimental reports.","One of the reports detailed research on children with Down syndrome. Mu Mian carefully examined its contents. Jiang Yinian and his team had attempted gene editing on fetuses diagnosed with Down syndrome, and Li Yan's child had been one of their subjects.","Gene editing on humans violated ethical guidelines and was strictly prohibited.","The cabinet also contained numerous reports documenting Jiang Yinian's illegal experiments, such as mind control through wearable devices, emotional deprivation experiments, human-animal hybrid gene experiments, and emotional inhibitors.","Mu Mian also found meeting notes detailing ongoing experiments, including one called the \"Genius Brain Project,\" which aimed to select students with low cognitive abilities and enhance their intelligence through drugs.","After a thorough search, Fang Rui and his team discovered that the villa had a basement. The entrance was hidden in a corner of the garden, secured with a locked door that required a passcode to open.","Fang Rui had brought along a professional locksmith. After inspecting the electronic lock, the technician sighed, \"This lock is connected to a self-destruct mechanism. I suspect there are explosives beneath the house. If we force our way in, it could trigger an explosion. We only have three attempts to enter the correct passcode. If we fail, the lock will permanently seal.\"","\"How many digits is the passcode?\" Mu Mian asked, noticing the keypad had both numbers and letters. It was likely a combination of both.","\"Probably five digits. It's unusual—most people wouldn't set such a short passcode.\"","Fang Rui theorized, \"The passcode is probably something of great importance to Jiang Yinian. Mu Mian, what do you think it could be?\"","Mu Mian pondered for a moment, \"The most important things to Yinian would be his research and his sister. Her English name is Sally, which is exactly five letters.\"","Mu Mian entered the five letters, but the smart lock emitted a harsh error tone.","She ran through everything Jiang Yinian might consider important but couldn't find anything that fit the criteria.","Wang suggested, \"Could it be a pinyin abbreviation? Though it doesn't seem to match the length.\"","\"Mu Mian, is there anything that connects both his research and your sister?\" Fang Rui prompted.","Suddenly, Mu Mian thought of her father's company. She entered five letters: SHEIN.","The lock clicked open.","Mu Mian explained, \"My father's pharmaceutical company is called SHEIN, which translates to 'Xiyin.'\"","A wide staircase led down to the basement. It was pitch dark, like a vast abyss ready to swallow everything whole.","Fang Rui shone his flashlight inside. The beam of light revealed a small child's body, preserved in formaldehyde.","As the light swept across the room, they saw various human specimens, a horrifying sight.","\"Where did these bodies come from? Did Jiang Yinian kill all these people?\" Wang whispered, his voice trembling.","No one could answer with certainty.","The young staff members were terrified. They had taken the job for the high salary, never imagining the villa concealed such gruesome secrets.","One of them stammered, \"We just started working here! We didn't do anything!\"","Fang Rui and his team decided not to venture further. Instead, they called for technicians to check for flammable or explosive materials and to test the air for toxic gases.","At that moment, Wang rushed in, holding his phone. \"Boss, it's bad news! Jiang Yinian has slipped away! He hired foreign bodyguards who attacked our surveillance team.\"","Fang Rui immediately called the chief to report the situation.","The chief coordinated with multiple departments to launch a joint operation to apprehend Jiang Yinian. Key transportation routes in Jiangzhou City were blocked, and teams were dispatched to monitor airports, high-speed rail stations, train stations, and highway checkpoints.","As they left Jiang Yinian's villa, Mu Mian couldn't shake a growing sense of unease.","She said, \"If Yinian knew we were coming to search the villa, why didn't he move the lab or at least take the documents with him? It's like he's given up trying to cover his tracks.\"","Fang Rui shared her doubts. He had always felt as though someone was guiding their investigation into Jiangmiao Group and the Neuro Rose. If such a person existed, who could it be? Could they have influenced Jiang Yinian's decisions?","\"Mu Mian, how was your sister's relationship with Jiang Yinian?\"","\"They used to be close, but after our father died, she grew to despise him.\"","\"And how did Jiang Yinian feel about your sister?\"","Mu Mian frowned, \"He said he loved her. But I don't know what kind of love he meant. The definition of love is too broad... Fang Rui, I should call my sister.\"","\"Go ahead.\"","Mu Mian dialed Shen Xiyin's number, but the call didn't go through.","\"Fang Rui, I can't reach her!\"","\"Don't panic. Do you have her friends' numbers? Try calling them.\"","\"No, I don't. Fang Rui, I've been so neglectful. I don't even have her friends' contacts.\"","Fang Rui reassured her, \"Mu Mian, don't be afraid. Let's go to her clinic and look for her.\"","When they arrived at the clinic, the receptionist told Mu Mian, \"Mu Mian, your sister received a call and ran out. Did something happen? I tried calling her, but her phone is off.\"","Fang Rui asked, \"How long ago did she leave?\"","\"About two hours ago.\"","\"Fang Rui, do you think my sister is dead?\" Mu Mian's mind was spinning, overwhelmed with fear. \"Chen Xue is dead. If my sister dies too, what will we do?\"","\"Mu Mian, we need to stay calm. It's possible Jiang Yinian has kidnapped her. If he loves her, he won't harm her. We're already searching the entire city for him. We'll find him soon.\"","The search operation was not going smoothly. Traffic surveillance cameras had initially captured Jiang Yinian's car, but upon investigation, it turned out the car was being driven by a designated driver. They then began analyzing surveillance footage from different areas, trying to trace Jiang Yinian's whereabouts.","Lin Sen also realized that something had happened to Shen Xiyin, and he immediately rushed to the clinic.","When he saw Mu Mian's tear-stained eyes, he was certain that Shen Xiyin had likely been kidnapped by Jiang Yinian.","Mu Mian choked back her sobs and said, \"I need to stay calm. My sister must have left us some clues.\"","They went to Shen Xiyin's office, where her desk was neatly organized, with no letters or notes left behind. The floor was also spotless, without a single scrap of paper.","Lin Sen noticed a painting on the floor and picked it up to examine it. The painting depicted a bright and vivid scene of the ocean and a sandy beach, the kind of artwork commonly used as decoration in therapy rooms.","Mu Mian said, \"Is my sister trying to tell us she went somewhere by the sea?\""]},{"number":216,"title":"Chapter 216: Neural Rose: Confrontation","paragraphs":["The sky had completely darkened, with no moon or stars in sight. The heavens were a heavy, oppressive black.","Shen Xiyin was escorted by two armed foreign bodyguards onto a small yacht.","Under the cover of night, the modest vessel was almost invisible.","Jiang Yinian stood on the yacht, smiling at Xiyin. \"Xiyin, I remember how much you love the ocean. The sea view in Jiangzhou City is beautiful, but it's a shame it's nighttime now. You can't see its splendor.\"","The ocean was pitch black, with waves glinting under the yacht's lights before vanishing into the night.","Shen Xiyin didn’t want to waste words with him. She immediately began searching the yacht but found no trace of Mu Mian. She rushed up to Jiang Yinian and demanded, \"Jiang Yinian, where is Mu Mian?\"","\"Mu Mian is safe. You wanted the police to find evidence of my crimes, so I sent that evidence to her.\"","Shen Xiyin breathed a sigh of relief and turned to leave, but the two bodyguards blocked her path.","\"Xiyin, I once promised you freedom. But now, I must break that promise,\" Jiang Yinian said, his expression pained. \"Why did you use the police to try and destroy me?\"","Jiang Yinian could accept that Shen Xiyin didn’t love him. He was content to love her alone. But why did she have to be so cruel, going to such lengths to ruin him?","Shen Xiyin shot back, \"Jiang Yinian, it was you who bribed my family’s nanny, wasn’t it? You used photos of Jiang Yun to lure Mu Mian back to the country. You instructed Chen Xue to befriend Mu Mian, only to hurt her. And you planned to continue experimenting on her. I won’t let you succeed.\"","\"I did all of this to fulfill your wish. Didn’t you always want Mu Mian to become 'normal'? But you’ve sheltered her too much. Her environment, her job, everything about her life was designed by you. In such a sheltered world, she could never grow. Look, in less than two years, Mu Mian has developed rich emotions. She’s even fallen in love.\"","\"I told you not to interfere with Mu Mian’s life.\"","\"So, you turned Director Chen against me? Bai Jing too, right? She actually stole my research reports for you. Xiyin, if you wanted the reports, why didn’t you just ask me? I would have given you anything, unconditionally.\"","\"So what if I did? I didn’t ask Bai Jing to steal from you. I didn’t need her to. She assumed I did and acted on her own. Jiang Yinian, you’re part of my father’s legacy. I have the right to dispose of you.\"","Shen Xiyin had used Bai Jing to reveal the truth about Neuro Rose to Director Chen. Director Chen had initially agreed to work with Jiang Yinian to save patients, but upon learning the truth, he completely broke down. Under Bai Jing’s influence, he killed two test subjects and staged their deaths as part of a serial murder case to draw police attention.","The patient with Down syndrome had severe congenital heart disease. Director Chen used high-frequency vibrations to trigger a heart attack, causing his death.","Yuan Yuan’s brain had already begun to deteriorate. Director Chen infected him with a virus that caused meningitis, accelerating his death.","Even if the police investigated further, they would find no connection to Shen Xiyin. Bai Jing had carried out everything, and she would never reveal the truth. Even if she did, there was no evidence to implicate Shen Xiyin.","Shen Xiyin said, \"I originally planned to use the Star Home case to eliminate you. But you were too well-hidden. I had to dismantle you from within.\"","In the Star Home case, Shen Xiyin first used Michelle, an autism therapist she had introduced to Jiang Yun, to drive a wedge between Lin Qianyan and Jiang Yun, deepening Lin Qianyan’s hatred for Jiang Yun.","Yuan Yuan often interacted with Lin Qianyan. Michelle used suggestive language to manipulate Yuan Yuan into drawing disturbing pictures, which he used to seek help from Li Min. Li Min, who already had severe psychological issues, orchestrated the murders of Director Zhang and Jiang Yun to protect the children.","Michelle had once been Shen Xiyin’s teacher and was now an employee at her therapy center. Michelle would never betray her.","Shen Xiyin had orchestrated everything from behind the scenes, exploiting everyone’s psychological weaknesses to achieve her goals. She left no trace.","Legally, she was completely innocent! She wouldn’t force Mu Mian to choose between her and Fang Rui, between justice and family.","Jiang Yinian protested, \"Do you still hate me for what happened to your parents? I didn’t cause their car accident. I respected your father like he was my own. How could I have harmed him?\"","The sea breeze tousled Shen Xiyin’s hair as she stood in the darkness, speaking softly, \"Jiang Yinian, I know it wasn’t you.\"","Jiang Yinian looked at her in shock. In an instant, he understood, and his heart ached even more.","\"They committed suicide! My father had been showing signs of Alzheimer’s. His memory was deteriorating, which is why he relied on you so much. When the drug he was developing failed, he lost all hope and decided to end his life.","My mother loved him deeply. She chose to die with him. My father didn’t want anyone to know about his illness or his suicide, so he staged an accident. That day, they deliberately crashed into a bridge, sending the car into the water.\"","\"Then why...\"","\"Why did the police think it was murder? Before they left, I cut the brake lines on their car to make it look like a murder... Don’t you see? I wanted to frame you, to force you out of the lab.\"","\"Why go through all that trouble? If you wanted me to leave, you could have just asked. You know I could never refuse you.\"","\"Jiang Yinian, I was getting revenge on you!\"","\"Why do you hate me so much?\"","\"Why do you think? You’re the one who told me about the Neuro Rose experiments. You’re the one who made me realize how monstrous my father was and the legacy of evil I inherited. You told me that Mu Mian’s recovery had nothing to do with me, that it was all because of Neuro Rose. You dragged me into hell, turning me into someone like you! Jiang Yinian, shouldn’t I hate you?\"","Shen Xiyin still remembered the crushing despair she felt when she learned the truth. Her world had been turned upside down. Her beloved father had been conducting illegal experiments on healthy people. She had always believed it was her selfless love and professional expertise that had helped Mu Mian recover, only to discover that Mu Mian’s progress was due to drugs.","She began to question everything—her family, her career—but the one thing she never doubted was how important Mu Mian was to her.","Later, she learned about Miao Miao and witnessed the devastating side effects of Neuro Rose. She had no choice but to inherit her father’s work and continue his research. She couldn’t let Mu Mian suffer the same fate. Even the slightest chance was worth any cost.","To her, Mu Mian was both family and her greatest professional achievement.","\"Xiyin, who told you Mu Mian was a test subject for Neuro Rose? I never said that. Mu Mian is not a test subject for Neuro Rose. I’m certain of that.\"","The sea wind howled, churning the waves and creating a cacophony of splashing sounds.","Shen Xiyin glared at Jiang Yinian in anger. \"I heard my father say it himself. He even mentioned giving Mu Mian an improved version of Neuro Rose. You knew full well how dangerous that drug is, how it accelerates brain deterioration. Mu Mian would have suffered and died like Miao Miao. Jiang Yinian, you’re complicit in this, and that’s why I’m going to destroy you!\"","\"But Mu Mian couldn’t have been a test subject for Neuro Rose. I’ve seen her brain scans. Her brain is perfectly healthy. Neuro Rose research was halted for over a decade. It wasn’t until after our research failed that your father had to restart it. There was no improved version of Neuro Rose back then.\"","The creator of Neuro Rose was Shen Xiyin’s aunt, Shen Min. Clinical trials revealed severe side effects, leading to the drug’s discontinuation.","Shen Xiyin’s pupils dilated as realization dawned on her."]},{"number":217,"title":"Chapter 217: Neural Rose: The Medicine Named Love","paragraphs":["“Shen Xiyin, Professor Shen lied to you. He likely said those things on purpose. He knew you cared about Mu Mian, so you would definitely inherit his laboratory and continue all his research for the sake of treating Mu Mian.”","Shen Xiyin’s father had once said that Jiang Yinian was not suitable for managing the laboratory—he was too capricious and lacked any moral boundaries. That’s why Shen Xiyin was the best candidate to inherit it. Jiang Yinian would help her unconditionally, and she had the ability to make everyone listen to her.","“That can’t be. My father wouldn’t lie to me. Jiang Yinian, you’re the one lying to me, aren’t you?”","Shen Xiyin couldn’t accept this. Her beloved father had deceived and manipulated her for the sake of his so-called research, forcing her to do what she disliked the most.","Her father knew how she felt about medical research—that she found it cruel. He also knew what her dreams were, yet he had ruthlessly stripped her of all that.","“Xiyin, you know I wouldn’t lie to you,” Jiang Yinian said. “Why don’t you believe that it was your love for Mu Mian, your refusal to give up, that created this miracle?”","“Autism can’t be cured! How could love alone make an autistic person normal? Jiang Yinian, tell me, you’re lying to me, aren’t you?”","“There have been many unexplained miracles in medical history. It wasn’t just your love for Mu Mian, but also your professional skills. And it wasn’t just you working alone—your parents, the therapists, they all worked hard too. Everyone loved Mu Mian. It was a miracle created by everyone together.”","“Then what do all these years mean? What does everything I’ve done mean?” Shen Xiyin’s world crumbled once again.","“Xiyin, Professor Shen wanted you to break the curse of your genes. What you’ve done isn’t meaningless. Once the effects of the Neural Rose are fully understood, there will be hope for treating many brain-related diseases. It will be another miracle in medical history.”","“I don’t want to create miracles!” Shen Xiyin collapsed to the ground, staring at her hands, hysterical. “What about all the experimental subjects who were sacrificed? The blood on my hands is there because of your lies. This is absurd!”","“Xiyin, the experiments you did abroad were nothing compared to what most pharmaceutical companies do. You have far more moral integrity than most. Ethics and morality are shackling the progress of science. True research should be free. It’s not us who are wrong!”","Tears streamed down Shen Xiyin’s face, but she forced herself to smile. This was nothing. Her world had crumbled many times before. At least Mu Mian wasn’t an experimental subject for the Neural Rose.","Jiang Yinian remembered once asking Shen Xiyin what her birthday wish was.","“I hope Mu Mian can become a normal person. I hope my father’s research succeeds. If I have to make three wishes, I hope everyone can be a little happier.”","“Don’t you want anything for yourself?”","“I already have so much. There’s nothing to regret.”","Back then, Shen Xiyin hadn’t met Lin Sen, hadn’t lost her parents, hadn’t taken over her father’s laboratory and pharmaceutical company. She didn’t yet know that her life would be filled with regrets.","“Xiyin, aren’t you afraid you’ll end up like your uncle, suffering from Alzheimer’s? You’ll forget everything, lose that brilliant mind of yours.”","The Shen family had a hereditary disease, a high likelihood of developing Alzheimer’s. That was why Jiang Yinian had researched the Neural Rose—he wanted to change Shen Xiyin’s fate.","“I’m a little afraid. That’s why I need to make sure Mu Mian becomes a normal person before I get sick. Once she can live independently, I’ll be at peace.”","“Why is Mu Mian so important to you?”","“She’s family. Family is important.”","At that moment, two bodyguards noticed faint lights flickering on the distant sea.","One of them said, “Boss, there’s a boat approaching us. We need to speed up and lose them. Can we accelerate?”","The bodyguard was confused. If they had been speeding up all along, they would have already boarded the cargo ship. The contact had prepared everything for them. Once they were on the ship, they could evade the police.","Jiang Yinian’s thoughts returned to the present. He didn’t respond to the bodyguard but instead looked down at Shen Xiyin. “I’m sorry. I should have told you the truth earlier. But I always thought that if you became like me, you’d love me.”","The bodyguard urged anxiously, “Boss, if we speed up now, we can still make it. Once we’re on the cargo ship, we’ll be safe.”","“Shen Xiyin, come with me, okay? Let’s fulfill your father’s dream together. We’ll make sure the world remembers him.”","Shen Xiyin wiped her tears and looked at him calmly. “Jiang Yinian, I won’t leave here alive with you.”","“If you die, Mu Mian will lose her sister.”","“If I leave with you, she’ll lose her sister all the same.”","“Boss, don’t hesitate, or we won’t be able to escape!” The bodyguard, hearing the sound of boat propellers in the distance, urged again.","“Shen Xiyin, will you remember me?”","“If the research makes progress, I’ll include your name and my father’s in the author credits of the paper. I’ll make sure the world remembers you both.”","Jiang Yinian gazed at her intently. “Shen Xiyin, I don’t need the world to remember me. I just want you to remember me.”","The police had cordoned off the Jiangzhou City docks and dispatched coast guard units to search the entire sea.","Fang Rui, Mu Mian, and Lin Sen boarded one of the boats, which also carried several snipers.","Soon, the sea surveillance system detected a yacht heading toward the area where cargo ships were docked. Once Jiang Yinian boarded one of those ships, the search would become much more complicated.","All the search boats closed in on the yacht.","Two armed bodyguards stood outside the yacht. Seeing the approaching boats, they opened fire.","Jiang Yinian, holding Shen Xiyin hostage, hid inside the cabin.","The sky and sea were pitch black, making visibility poor. It took the snipers a while to aim, but they eventually shot one of the bodyguards.","The other bodyguard quickly took cover behind the boat.","Concerned for the hostage, the police didn’t dare to advance recklessly, and the situation reached a stalemate.","Soon, reinforcements arrived, surrounding the yacht. The remaining bodyguard was also shot by the snipers.","Fearing that Jiang Yinian might harm the hostage, the boats stopped ten meters away, not daring to get closer.","Jiang Yinian took a pistol from a drawer and, with Shen Xiyin as his hostage, stepped out of the cabin. He shouted to Fang Rui, “Let me leave safely, or I’ll kill her!”","Shen Xiyin said, “Fang Rui, just shoot. Don’t worry about me!”","Fang Rui, while directing the snipers to aim at Jiang Yinian, tried to negotiate. “Don’t harm the hostage. What do you need to leave safely?”","“I need a helicopter!”","Fang Rui replied, “Okay, but it will take time to prepare. Don’t harm the hostage in the meantime.”","Jiang Yinian leaned close to Shen Xiyin’s ear and whispered, “Shen Xiyin, if you hadn’t met Lin Sen, would you have loved me?”","“No.”","“But I met you first.”","“Jiang Yinian, the answer is still no.”","Jiang Yinian’s movements exposed his head.","Taking advantage of his distraction, a sniper quickly aimed and fired. The bullet pierced through the air, striking Jiang Yinian squarely in the forehead.","Warm blood splattered onto Shen Xiyin’s face.","Jiang Yinian slowly collapsed, his memories flashing back to the past.","“Jiang Yinian, you seem lonely. Can I be your friend?”","“Jiang Yinian, you’re like Mu Mian—you’re a genius. Geniuses are different from everyone else.”","“Jiang Yinian, even though you’re a genius, you can’t always look down on others. Intelligence is determined by genes. You’re lucky to have a high IQ, but you can’t despise those who aren’t as smart. That’s unfair.”","“Jiang Yinian, you can’t let your dark thoughts become reality. You need to be a good person. Can’t control yourself? Then I’ll keep an eye on you from now on!”","“Jiang Yinian, I’ve fallen for someone. I’m going to tell him. Wish me luck!”","\"Jiang Yinian, even if I become like you, I could never like you.\"","Jiang Yinian looked into Shen Xiyin's beautiful eyes. They seemed to glisten with tears, yet also seemed dry. He slowly closed his eyes.","\"Sister, I'm so glad you're okay!\" Mu Mian ran from the boat to Shen Xiyin's side, wrapping her arms tightly around her. \"You can't die! If you die, I'd have to make myself a schizophrenic just to keep a version of you alive in my mind.\"","\"Mu Mian, I know, and that's why I won't die so easily.\"","\"Sister, I'm still so scared.\"","Shen Xiyin held Mu Mian tightly in return. There was a time when she was afraid every day—afraid that Mu Mian would become another Miao Miao, afraid of losing her. But now, she was no longer afraid. Mu Mian would live a healthy life, full of happiness and joy.","Fang Rui stared at Jiang Yinian's lifeless body, a sudden wave of panic washing over him.","Jiang Yinian was dead. Did that mean all the secrets about the Neuro Rose would be lost? Was Mu Mian an experiment of the Neuro Rose?","If Mu Mian turned out like Miao Miao, what would he do?"]},{"number":218,"title":"Chapter 218: Neural Rose: Case Closed","paragraphs":["In that villa, a lot of incriminating evidence was found, enough to convict Jiang Yinian.","Jiang Yinian's illegal experiments also implicated many industries under the Jiangmiao Group. The hospitals and high-end nursing homes under his name were also shut down.","However, they did not find the list of Jiang Yinian's accomplices. The evidence in the villa could only point to Jiang Yinian, but not his accomplices.","The materials found in his laboratory did not include experimental data on the \"Neural Rose,\" nor any information about it. After Jiang Yinian's death, everything about the Neural Rose became a mystery.","Jiang Yinian's death brought down the Jiangmiao Group, but would the people behind him continue their criminal activities?","Jiang Yinian had prepared his will long ago, leaving all his assets to Lin Qianyan.","Lin Qianyan was still a minor, but Jiang Yinian had cultivated a large number of loyal followers during his lifetime and established strict management systems to ensure that the operations of the Lin family would not be significantly affected by the change of heir. These loyal individuals handled Jiang Yinian's inheritance for Lin Qianyan.","After the conclusion of Jiang Yinian's case, Fang Rui went to the clinic where Shen Xiyin worked to find her.","The receptionist looked upset and said to Fang Rui, \"Officer Fang, Sister Xiyin is resigning. You and Mu Mian should try to convince her not to leave. We’ll all miss her so much.\"","Fang Rui walked to the door of Shen Xiyin's office and knocked.","\"Come in.\"","Shen Xiyin was packing her things, as it was her last day at work. She wasn’t surprised to see Fang Rui.","\"Fang Rui, I knew you’d come to see me.\"","\"Sister Xiyin, do you really know nothing about the Neural Rose?\"","Shen Xiyin looked at Fang Rui seriously. \"If Mu Mian were to become like Miao Miao, would you still love her unconditionally?\"","\"I would. No matter what happens to her, I’ll stay by her side,\" Fang Rui clenched his fists.","Ever since he learned about the existence of the Neural Rose and Miao Miao's tragic fate, he had been living in fear. What if Mu Mian was also a subject of the Neural Rose experiment? What if she turned out like Miao Miao? What would he do?","Shen Xiyin continued, \"What if she were to die soon, just like Miao Miao?\"","Fang Rui finally understood why Miao Miao's boyfriend had committed suicide after her death. He loved her too much and couldn’t bear to live without her.","\"I don’t know. Maybe I’d die with her, or maybe I’d live on to remember her.\"","Shen Xiyin smiled. \"Then whether Mu Mian is a subject of the Neural Rose experiment doesn’t matter anymore, does it?\"","Fang Rui felt a surge of intense fear. \"Sister Xiyin, is Mu Mian really...?\"","\"She’s not! If she were an experiment, she’d be an experiment of love. It’s the love of all of us, our refusal to give up, that created this miracle. And you, along with Mu Mian’s friends, will continue to carry on this miracle.\"","Fang Rui’s face lit up with joy, but he sensed the underlying meaning in Shen Xiyin’s words. \"What about you?\"","\"I’m leaving. Mu Mian doesn’t need me anymore, so it’s time for me to pursue my own dreams.\" Mu Mian had been the most important person in her life, and she always would be, but Shen Xiyin had other important things to do.","In the past, she had done everything for Mu Mian. From now on, she would do it for herself and to save more patients.","Fang Rui couldn’t help but ask, \"Sister Xiyin, were you the one guiding us in investigating the Jiangmiao Group all along?\"","\"Fang Rui, if you want to continue investigating this matter, you can. But in the end, you won’t find any evidence.","You don’t have to make difficult choices—whether to investigate or not, to uphold justice or ignore some evils. But please don’t tell Mu Mian about your suspicions. I want to remain the kind older sister in her memories.\"","Fang Rui had once investigated Shen Xiyin’s connection to the cases but found no clues.","\"Fang Rui, there’s a psychological dilemma called the trolley problem: There are two railway tracks. On one track, there’s one person tied up, and on the other, there are five. A train is speeding toward them. You have a button that can switch the train’s direction. Which track would you choose?\"","Fang Rui knew Shen Xiyin was hinting at something. The track with five people represented the victims of the Jiangmiao Group, while the track with one person represented those sacrificed to bring down the group.","\"What if the five people were replaced by fifty, five hundred, or even countless people? Would the choice still be difficult?\"","Fang Rui said, \"I could choose not to press the button.\"","\"Wouldn’t you feel guilty for not pressing it? People would still die, whether it’s one person or five. The train has to run over one of the tracks.\"","This was one of the reasons Shen Xiyin wanted to destroy the Jiangmiao Group. They were too insane and had no moral boundaries.","Jiang Yinian used his resources to lure many doctors and researchers into helping him with illegal experiments. Older figures like Director Chen, who had encountered too many incurable patients, harbored intense psychological conflicts and longed for new treatment methods. So when Jiang Yinian told them he could break through the current limitations, they joined him without hesitation.","Younger individuals like Chen Xue always wanted to surpass their elders. Jiang Yinian gave them the opportunity to stand on equal footing with their predecessors and even provided them with more resources. As a result, they were even more loyal to Jiang Yinian than their elders.","But as long as Jiang Yinian, the mastermind, was dead, the others wouldn’t be able to cause any more trouble.","Shen Xiyin smiled. \"Fang Rui, the optimal solution is to have someone else press the button for you. That way, you won’t face moral condemnation.\"","Fang Rui understood that Shen Xiyin was implying that everything had been done by others on her behalf, leaving no evidence.","\"Fang Rui, I hope you’ll take good care of Mu Mian for me.\"","\"I will.\"","Fang Rui drove back to find Mu Mian. He rushed into her office, where she was reaching for a file on the top shelf of a cabinet. Fang Rui ran over and hugged her tightly.","\"Mu Mian, I was so scared that you might also be a subject of the Neural Rose experiment, that you might end up like Miao Miao. But thankfully, you’re not.\" Fang Rui held her tightly.","Mu Mian frowned, puzzled. \"Fang Rui, you’re so silly. How could I possibly be a subject of the Neural Rose experiment? I’m a genius. No drug could create someone like me. Besides, I regularly check my brain scans, and they’ve always been healthy.","\"Fang Rui, don’t you remember I’m a medical professional? If someone injected me with drugs or made me take strange medications, how could I not notice? Have you become less intelligent?\"","Fang Rui didn’t respond.","After a while, Mu Mian reminded him, \"Fang Rui, you’re hugging me too tightly. I can barely breathe.\"","Fang Rui only held her tighter, as if this could dispel the fear he had been suppressing all this time.","\"Fang Rui, you’ve been hugging for too long... Okay, just a little longer... Really, it’s been a long time.\"","Wang, watching them, suddenly thought of Chen Shu. He felt a pang of sadness but quickly forced a smile. Life goes on. People will leave, but others will always come.","After the case was closed, Lin Qianyan went to the police station with his bodyguards and personal assistant. As a relative, he was allowed to claim Jiang Yinian’s body.","Mu Mian led Lin Qianyan into the freezer and helped him locate Jiang Yinian’s corpse.","Lin Qianyan said to Mu Mian, \"Mu Mian, my cousin Jiang Yinian didn’t lose to you. He lost to himself.\"","When Jiang Yinian realized that Shen Xiyin had orchestrated everything, he gave up resisting. Lin Qianyan didn’t understand why Jiang Yinian, such a cold-blooded person, could love so irrationally. But Lin Qianyan took this as a lesson: he would never fall in love with anyone in the future!","\"If Jiang Yinian hadn’t committed crimes, he would have been a medical genius,\" Mu Mian said regretfully.","Lin Qianyan countered, \"Even as a criminal, he still was.\"","\"Lin Qianyan, can’t you try to be a good person?\"","Lin Qianyan didn’t answer. Only naive people divide others into good and bad. In the real world, the lines are much more complex. Criminals aren’t necessarily bad people, and those praised and supported aren’t necessarily good.","His bodyguards helped him load the body into a car.","Lin Qianyan looked at Jiang Yinian's lifeless body and sneered, \"Yinian, I told you she didn't love you. You were such a fool. Now, you're dead. She'll forget you, she'll be happy with someone else, and you’ll get nothing!\"","\"Qianyan, are we heading to the funeral home now?\" the assistant asked cautiously.","\"No, I’m taking Yinian home.\"","\"But what about Mr. Jiang’s remains?\"","\"I’m going to have him frozen. Help me find someone to build a cryogenic chamber, like the ones in sci-fi movies.\"","The assistant was too shocked to speak. After a moment, she managed to say, \"Qianyan, you should let Mr. Jiang rest in peace.\"","Lin Qianyan murmured softly, \"I never liked cold corpses before, but now I’ll have to learn to.\"","\"You can’t like a corpse!\"","\"But I want to see him! I can’t bring Yinian back to life now, but that doesn’t mean I never will.\"","\"Qianyan, the dead can’t come back to life!\"","\"Medicine and technology are always advancing. What’s impossible now might not be impossible in the future.\""]},{"number":219,"title":"Chapter 219: 52Hz Whale and Her Island (Main Text Complete)","paragraphs":["The sky was a clear, unblemished blue, the sun was radiant, and a gentle breeze caressed the earth.","Mu Mian and Fang Rui went to the airport to see Shen Xiyin off.","When Mu Mian found out that Shen Xiyin was leaving, she was deeply saddened. But then she remembered the words of her sister’s friend: her sister deserved to live her own life.","In the past, Mu Mian had stood in the way of her sister’s dreams, but now she knew she had to respect her sister’s choices.","Mu Mian had considered going back with Shen Xiyin, but Shen Xiyin had refused.","“Mu Mian, even though we’ll be apart, we’ll always be family. Whenever you need me, I’ll be there for you. You’ll always be the person I love and care about the most.”","“What about Lin Sen?”","“He’s third.”","“What’s second?”","Shen Xiyin patted Mu Mian’s head and changed the subject. “When you and Fang Rui get married, I’ll come back for your wedding.”","Mu Mian whispered, “But he hasn’t proposed to me yet.”","“You could propose to him.”","“He already said no.”","Shen Xiyin smiled. “That was before, wasn’t it?”","As the boarding time approached, Shen Xiyin said to Mu Mian, “Goodbye, Mu Mian!”","“Goodbye, sister!”","Shen Xiyin glanced around the crowd. Lin Sen hadn’t come to see her off. But she had already prepared herself for this. She had hurt Lin Sen again, and it was her own fault.","Once on the plane, Shen Xiyin turned off her phone. She took out a book, flipping through it restlessly, but couldn’t focus on a single word. Just then, she noticed someone standing by her seat.","“Shen Xiyin.”","She looked up and saw Lin Sen.","Lin Sen sat down beside her and handed her a folder.","Shen Xiyin flipped through the documents, her expression changing as she read. The files contained information about her pharmaceutical company abroad, detailing their recent research projects.","Lin Sen knew everything now, including her true nature.","Shen Xiyin looked at Lin Sen and said, “Lin Sen, these things aren’t illegal abroad. My lawyer can get me out of this.”","Lin Sen remained silent, simply sitting beside her.","“Lin Sen, the plane is about to take off. If you want to leave, there’s still time.”","Lin Sen didn’t speak. Instead, he reached out and tightly grasped Shen Xiyin’s hand.","“Lin Sen, are you taking me back?”","In the vast blue sky, a plane soared past, leaving a long trail behind it.","Chen Xue’s mother held a funeral for her.","The funeral was lively, with most of her colleagues from the bureau attending. However, they had kept it a secret from Zhang Qiang.","After learning that Zhang Qiang had lost his memory, his parents had hidden everything related to Chen Xue, locking it away in a cabinet. Photos and videos had also been deleted.","Midway through the funeral, Zhang Qiang suddenly appeared, holding a bouquet of yellow chrysanthemums.","Wang, visibly nervous, asked, “Zhang Qiang, why are you here?”","“You’re all so unfair. Chen Xue was my colleague. How could you not invite me to her funeral?” Zhang Qiang’s parents didn’t want him to miss Chen Xue’s funeral, so they had told him about it.","Everyone breathed a sigh of relief. Li turned to Wang and said, “Wang, how could you forget to inform Zhang Qiang?”","“Ah, I just forgot!”","Zhang Qiang placed the bouquet of chrysanthemums in front of Chen Xue’s grave.","“Chen Xue, rest in peace.”","Chen Xue’s mother and relatives wept bitterly, while the other colleagues were also deeply saddened. Zhang Qiang looked at Chen Xue’s portrait, seemingly emotionless.","After the funeral, Zhang Qiang returned home as if nothing had happened. Once he locked the door, he covered his mouth and burst into tears.","He turned on his computer and found a story on a website. He had lost his memory, but he had written a novel about his and Chen Xue’s story. They were the main characters, so the plot was simple, and it had almost no readers.","But the emotions in the story were genuine. As he read the words, memories seemed to flood back into his mind.","Using his novel as a guide, he found a social media account called “The Happy Life of the Little Forensic Scientist and the Little Police Officer.” There were only a few videos, but in them, Chen Xue and he were deeply in love. Back then, they had pretended to be a couple to catch a serial killer targeting couples, and through that, they had truly fallen in love.","But he didn’t want anyone to know that he still loved Chen Xue. He didn’t want them to feel sorry for him.","The fact that he loved Chen Xue was something only he needed to know.","He would strive to live happily, because that’s what Chen Xue would have wanted.","After the case was closed, the bureau chief gave Fang Rui and Mu Mian a long vacation.","Mu Mian and Fang Rui went on a trip.","“Fang Rui, there’s a museum with a very beautiful mummy called the Loulan Beauty. Let’s go there.”","“Okay.”","They flew to a northern city and found the museum. Since it was a weekday, there weren’t many people inside. Mu Mian wasn’t interested in the other artifacts and went straight to the Loulan Beauty exhibit.","The Loulan Beauty lay in a glass display, her skin wrinkled and dried. To most people, she held no beauty, but Mu Mian could see from her bones that she had once been a beautiful woman.","After a while, Mu Mian bent down and rummaged through her bag.","“Mu Mian, what are you looking for?”","“Found it.”","Mu Mian pulled out a photo of Chen Xue from her bag. She held the photo up to the mummy and whispered, “Chen Xue, you said you’d take me to see the Loulan Beauty. Now, we’ve seen her together. She’s truly beautiful. It’s just a shame that only your photo is here with me. Chen Xue, I’ll never forget you.”","Mu Mian’s voice choked with emotion.","Fang Rui hugged her, offering silent comfort.","As their vacation neared its end, Fang Rui took Mu Mian to the largest aquarium in Jiangzhou City.","They watched the penguins, the dolphin show, and the colorful tropical fish. Finally, Fang Rui led Mu Mian to the whale exhibit.","There was a beautiful beluga whale, happily playing with other fish. It opened its mouth, swallowing the smaller fish, only to spit them out moments later.","Mu Mian loved the whale and enthusiastically greeted it.","Fang Rui said, “Mu Mian, do you remember the story of the 52Hz whale you told me?”","“Yes, but this isn’t the 52Hz whale. It has many friends. That lonely whale has already disappeared into the deep sea.”","“Mu Mian, you once said that people with autism are like the 52Hz whale. Your frequency is different from others, so it’s hard to connect with them. I can’t become another 52Hz whale, but I’ll try my best to be the island you can rely on.”","Mu Mian stared at Fang Rui in surprise.","Fang Rui pulled a ring from his pocket. “Mu Mian, will you marry me and let me be your island?” His voice trembled slightly.","Zhang, Wang, and Li suddenly appeared out of nowhere, cheering, “Mu Mian, say yes! Say yes!”","Mu Mian extended her finger and softly said, “I will.”","Fang Rui slipped the ring onto her finger and then held her tightly.","“Fang Rui, can I ask you something now?”","“What is it?”","“After you die, will I legally own your body?”","“...Yes.”","“What if your parents don’t give it to me?”","“Then I’ll sign a body donation form for you.”","“Can you sign it now?” Mu Mian pulled a body donation form from the corner of her backpack and handed it to Fang Rui.","The group of friends who had been cheering them on was stunned. They couldn’t help but mutter, “Mu Mian really never gives up, does she?”","Fang Rui sighed and signed the form.","“Fang Rui, I love you so much, so very much. It’s not because I want your body. I love you, and wanting your body is just an added bonus.”","“I know. Mu Mian, I love you too.”","“You only said ‘love’ once.”","“Mu Mian, I love you, love you, love you.”","Behind them, the beluga whale swam back and forth, scattering the colorful fish like bursts of fireworks in the water.","Mu Mian, the 52Hz whale who had once lost connection with the world, might never find another whale with the same frequency. But it didn’t matter anymore—she had found her island.","The End.","Congratulations on finishing the story!"]},{"number":220,"title":"Chapter 220: Shen Xi Yin Extras: The Meaning of Love","paragraphs":["Upon entering high school, Shen Xiyin was plagued by a dilemma: What is the meaning of life?","At that time, she voraciously read a lot of philosophical books and suddenly realized that life was dull, drab, and meaningless—dull, drab, meaningless. Human beings will eventually die, and at the moment of death, everything they possessed becomes meaningless to the deceased.","Her friends did not understand her confusion. They found life to be very meaningful, pursuing their passions vigorously—romantic relationships full of fervor, participating in various activities, or preparing for university applications...","But Shen Xiyin didn't have such strong desires. She could effortlessly attain whatever she wanted, had no dreams, and could not comprehend the meaning of life.","It was around this time that Mu Mian came to her home.","Shen's Father told her, \"Xiyin, little Mian is going to live with us from now on. Do you mind?\"","\"Not at all.\"","This was her second encounter with Mu Mian. The first time she met Mu Mian, she was still a chubby baby. Now, though older, Mu Mian appeared like a soul-less doll, indifferent and unresponsive to the outside world.","Shen Xiyin approached Mu Mian, offering her a piece of chocolate, \"Little Mian, hello. Welcome to my home.\"","Mu Mian lowered her head, staring at the patterns on the floor, offering no response.","In that moment, Shen Xiyin realized that Mu Mian might not be a normal child.","Shen's Father told Shen Xiyin, \"Xiyin, little Mu Mian might have to live with us permanently from now on. You two should get along well.\"","\"Dad, will Uncle Mu also be living with us?\"","The expression on Shen's Father's face became slightly unnatural, \"He has something important to attend to.\"","\"Alright.\"","Soon, Shen Xiyin learned that Mu Mian was a child with autism.","Mu Mian didn't speak, never made eye contact, disliked physical contact, but she was also very obedient. Her way of resisting others was to sneakily hide in the closet.","Upon arriving at the Shen family's home, Mu Mian wouldn't eat, drink, or sleep. Whenever no one was watching, she would crawl into the wardrobe.","The Shen family were at their wits' end with Mu Mian's behavior, and even the nanny was on the verge of resigning from the constant hassle. Everyone was on the brink of losing patience.","When Shen Xiyin returned home from school, she found that Mu Mian was missing. She searched the room for a while before finally pulling open the wardrobe door, only to meet the gaze of darkened eyes and a slight upturned mouth.","Mu Mian was smiling at her. Her smile was stiff, but her eyes sparkled.","Mu Mian glanced at Shen Xiyin, quickly averted her eyes, and her smile faded from her small face—her expectations were unfulfilled, as this was not the person she had hoped for.","Shen Xiyin suddenly understood something and inquired, \"Little Mian, are you waiting for your dad?\"","Previously, Shen Xiyin had always assumed that Mu Mian lived in her own world, much like being enclosed within a glass dome, isolated from the outside world.","But in that instant, Shen Xiyin realized that perhaps Mu Mian could perceive the outside world, just not in the way a normal person would.","Mu Mian didn't answer. She shrank back into the closet, hiding herself in the darkness, finding comfort there.","Shen Xiyin felt that the closet was like another world, with only Mu Mian, alone in the darkness.","\"Little Mian, you must be hungry. Wait a moment, I'll get you something to eat.\"","Shen Xiyin wasn't sure what Mu Mian liked to eat, so she grabbed a bit of everything they had at home—snacks, fruits—placing them on the floor in front of the closet.","\"Little Mian, come out and have a bite, okay?\"","Mu Mian still showed no response.","Shen Xiyin waited for a long time, but Mu Mian didn't come out. She had no choice but to run and find her father.","\"Dad, has Uncle Mu abandoned Little Mian? She's very sad, continuously waiting for her father to come and pick her up.\"","Shen's father's expression was complicated: \"Your Uncle Mu has gone to a faraway place. He is unable to care for Little Mian.\"","\"Is he... deceased?\"","\"Yes.\"","Shen Xiyin found Mu Mian utterly pitiful. She had no father; the only person who could understand and take care of her was gone.","\"Dad, what will become of Little Mian?\" Without the mediator through which she communicated with the world, she could only live alone, trapped in her own world.","Mu Mian was pitiful!","\"I promised your Uncle Mu that I would find the best therapists and provide her with intervention treatments. Xiyin, she will be your sister from now on. We have to take good care of her together.\"","\"Dad, I will!\"","The next day, Shen Xiyin discovered that one of the soufflé cakes she had placed on the floor was missing, as were a few strawberries.","A sudden happiness swelled within her—Little Mian had accepted her food.","\"Little Mian, do you like this kind of cake and strawberries?\"","Mu Mian didn't respond to her.","Shen Xiyin helped Mu Mian unpack her luggage, where she found a notebook inside, recording some of Mu Mian's habits:","For example, upon arriving in a new environment, she had to be guided to inspect the environment repeatedly, over and over, until she was confident that the place was safe and no longer showed signs of stress.","Mu Mian cared little about the taste of food but had high standards for its appearance; she wouldn't eat sliced cucumbers but adored diced ones.","Bringing Mu Mian to the bathroom, she would wash herself, but the water temperature had to be strictly between 35 and 37°C.","Mu Mian enjoyed playing hide-and-seek and liked hiding in the closet. However, just knocking on the cabinet door three times would coax her out. This was her secret signal with her father.","Mu Mian disliked any physical contact. If one wanted to hold her hand, she must be given gloves to wear...","Shen Xiyin realized that this notebook was like a codebook, decoding Mu Mian's thoughts. She wondered about the tremendous effort Uncle Mu must have gone through to compile this information.","Mu Mian had a father who deeply loved her.","Shen Xiyin recalled the last time she had seen Uncle Mu; he had recently gotten a divorce, looking gaunt and desperate, reluctantly approaching her father to borrow money.","At that time, Shen Xiyin hadn't known that Mu Mian had autism, entrusting Uncle Mu to give Mu Mian a doll.","\"Xiyin, Mu Mian doesn't like dolls. But thank you anyway,\" Uncle Mu had said with a bitter smile.","\"What kind of toy does she like?\"","\"Right now, I don't know. Mu Mian has no favorite toys.\"","\"I will ask her the next time I see her.\"","Shen Xiyin felt sad, for she would never see Uncle Mu again.","Shen Xiyin went to the cabinet, following the instructions in the notebook by knocking on the closet door three times:","Knock, knock, knock.","When the third sound echoed, Mu Mian crawled out of the cabinet.","Seeing Shen Xiyin, the light in Mu Mian's eyes dimmed, and she tried to retreat back into the closet. But Shen Xiyin said, \"Little Mian, your father entrusted me with taking care of you. From now on, I am your big sister.\"","Mu Mian didn't reply, but she didn't return to the cupboard.","\"Don't you believe me?\" Shen Xiyin knocked three times on the cabinet door again, \"Look, I know your secret signal with your father. Do you believe me now?\"","Mu Mian still didn't answer, but after a few seconds, she nodded her head.","Shen Xiyin was delighted—Mu Mian could understand her speech. This meant that Mu Mian's world was not entirely closed after all.","\"Little Mian, sister will accompany you to explore this house, alright?\"","Mu Mian remained silent.","Shen Xiyin slipped gloves onto Mu Mian's hands and then led Mu Mian to inspect the room, prying the girl away from her closet.","\"This will be your room from now on, little Mian. Do you like it?\"","The room's decor was an exact replica of Mu Mian's former home, causing no disruption for the girl who inspected every corner meticulously.","\"Now let's go outside and take a look. Don't be afraid—big sister is here to protect you.\"","Shen Xiyin led Mu Mian to inspect the exterior corridor.","Mu Mian moved slowly, taking great care to examine each tile, each piece of furniture, retracing her steps and revisiting things over and over.","Shen Xiyin patiently accompanied Mu Mian in her inspection, documenting areas that seemed uncomfortable for her.","They had spent four hours studying every nook and cranny of the Shen family's home.","\"Little Mu Mian, this house will be your new home from now on, a home where you will abide forever,\" Shen Xiyin assured.","Mu Mian turned her head toward Shen Xiyin, apparently inquiring, what about my father?","\"Mu Mian, when you are grown, your father will return,\" Shen Xiyin lied with a kind heart.","Methodically, the girl with gloves reached out, slowly grasping Shen Xiyin’s hand in her gloved one.","Shen Xiyin smiled and said, “Mian, you’ve accepted this place, haven’t you?”","Mu Mian patted her stomach.","“Are you hungry? Let’s go eat.”","Mu Mian gradually adapted to her life in the Shen family, but she seemed to only understand what Shen Xiyin said. She rarely responded to anyone else.","Shen's father had hired many therapists for Mu Mian. When they evaluated her, she would sit there like a lifeless puppet, not giving any responses, leading to extremely poor test results.","“She is the most severe case of autism I’ve ever seen.”","“Her condition is very bad. Her intellectual level is low, her sensory integration is severely disordered, and she’s already six years old, yet she still hasn’t spoken a single word. She has missed the optimal period for language development... You need to prepare yourselves. Intervention therapy at this point won’t bring much improvement.”","Shen's father showed little reaction to this news, as he had expected such a result. However, since he had promised Mu Wenzhou that he would take good care of Mu Mian, he would continue to provide her with the best intervention therapy, even if there was no hope of improvement.","Upon hearing the therapist’s words, Shen Xiyin quietly but firmly expressed her dissatisfaction: “You don’t know enough about Mian. How can you say her condition is so bad without truly understanding her?”","“But I’ve dealt with many autistic patients. I know their condition well.”","“Everyone is unique, and every autistic person is unique. You can’t just base your diagnosis on your experience.”","The therapist looked at Shen's father: “If you doubt my professional capabilities, why did you hire me in the first place? I’m sure other therapists have said the same thing.”","Shen Xiyin stared at him and said, each word clear: “So, you’re fired!”","Shen Xiyin suddenly found something she desperately wanted to achieve: she wanted to become a therapist herself. She wanted to make Mu Mian normal.","“Xiyin, you can’t be so disrespectful!”","The therapist was actually a friend of Shen Xiyin’s father. Shen's Father quickly apologized and escorted him out.","Shen Xiyin decided to go home and look up information about autism but saw Mu Mian standing motionless at the corner of the corridor.","Shen Xiyin walked over to Mu Mian and crouched down to look at her. “Did you hear what we just said, Mian?”","Mu Mian didn’t respond.","“You understand, don’t you?”","Mu Mian still didn’t respond.","“He’s wrong! There’s nothing wrong with not speaking. People don’t always need to communicate through words. You don’t speak, and yet I know what you’re thinking. You want to eat strawberries, don’t you?”","Mu Mian glanced at Shen Xiyin and shook her head.","“You want to build with blocks?”","Mu Mian continued to shake her head.","“Do you want to play hide and seek?”","Mu Mian paused for a moment and then shook her head.","“Mian, are you missing your dad?”","Mu Mian didn’t nod, nor did she shake her head. She had no idea what “missing” was. All she knew was that someone very important to her was gone.","“Don’t be afraid, Mian. I’ll always be with you.” Shen Xiyin promised.","Later, Mu Mian gradually forgot about her father.","One day, Mu Mian spoke her first words: “Sister, I’m hungry.”","Mu Mian started going to school.","Mu Mian made her first friend, though the friend had been bribed by Shen Xiyin.","Eventually, Mu Mian found something she liked.","One day, the nanny said to Shen Xiyin: “Xiyin, Mian was playing with the corpse of a small animal. Could there be something wrong with her psychology?”","“Mian likes corpses? That’s great, she’s finally found something she likes.” Shen Xiyin’s expression was calm.","Aunt Zhang grabbed Shen Xiyin, her face filled with fear: “Xiyin, but Mian likes corpses!”","“Aunt Zhang, there’s nothing wrong with liking corpses. Mian likes corpses, so she can pursue a career that legally allows her to interact with them. She can become a forensic scientist, a specimen maker, a butcher, an undertaker, or even work at a mortuary...”","The nanny left in resignation.","Just then, Mu Mian walked over and handed Shen Xiyin a box: “Sister, gift, for you.”","Shen Xiyin opened the box and inside was a specimen of a small hamster.","“It’s cute, isn’t it?” Mu Mian looked up, proudly.","“Yes. But you can only turn corpses into specimens. You can’t harm living things.”","“I’ll remember. Sister, when you die, I’ll turn you into a specimen too. That way, you’ll exist forever.”","“That’s fine with me!”","Shen Xiyin felt she had found the meaning of her life.","But only much later did Shen Xiyin realize that this had all been a trap. Mu Mian was the bait, and her father had used this trap to ensnare her entire life."]},{"number":221,"title":"Chapter 221: Extra Episode: Lin Qianyan's Extra Episode - No One Loves Me","paragraphs":["Lin Qianyan learned to speak at the age of six, but long before that, he had learned to think and had already realized that his parents did not love him.","Because of his delayed language development and introverted personality, therapists had early on labeled him as autistic.","After learning to speak, Lin Qianyan still rarely spoke, because he disliked language and despised talking to the foolish people around him.","They always spoke to him in cutesy, childish ways, using baby words and silly tones. Lin Qianyan had no interest in responding to them.","He continued to pretend to be autistic, so he could avoid going to school and dealing with these stupid people.","His annoying father had passed away when he was very young, and his mother, Jiang Yun, occasionally visited him, but she was often impatient and showed visible disgust on her face.","Jiang Yun believed he was autistic and couldn’t interpret her expressions.","But autistic people aren’t idiots, and besides, he wasn’t autistic—he was a genius.","It was his cousin, Jiang Yinian, who told him he was a genius.","When Lin Qianyan was ten, Jiang Yinian’s company ran into trouble and he needed a lot of money. At first, Jiang Yun refused to invest, but Jiang Yinian convinced her by proposing a project for autistic treatment.","After that, Jiang Yun would bring Jiang Yinian with her whenever she visited Lin Qianyan. Jiang Yun admired him, and they often discussed various matters, with Jiang Yun occasionally showing approval.","Lin Qianyan grew furious. This sudden cousin had stolen the little attention Jiang Yun had previously given him.","Lin Qianyan decided to get revenge.","He slipped a blade into Jiang Yinian’s shoe when no one was looking, planning for Jiang Yinian to get cut and bleed all over his feet when he changed back into his own shoes.","Lin Qianyan enjoyed gore and violence, the sight of broken, dismembered bodies. These motifs frequently appeared in his drawings.","“Lin Qianyan, what are you doing?”","Just as Lin Qianyan placed the blade, he saw Jiang Yinian standing behind him.","Jiang Yinian glanced at the shoe in his hand. “Lin Qianyan, one can do bad things, but they must not get caught. Otherwise, it’s a foolish crime.”","Lin Qianyan glared at him. “So what if I get caught? My mother can smooth things over for me. Even if I killed you, I wouldn’t be punished. I’m a kid, autistic. The law can’t touch me.”","“I could also kill you. As long as no one knows it was me, I won’t be punished either.”","Lin Qianyan backed away in fear.","Jiang Yinian seemed to understand what was causing his anger. “Lin Qianyan, don’t worry. I won’t take your mother’s love away from you.”","“You’re the kind of son she wanted. But it doesn’t matter. I don’t need her love. I just don’t like you coming here. I hate you.”","“She treats me well because I have value. This world works that way. There’s no such thing as unconditional love. If you want her to love you, you need to show her your value.”","“I have no value.”","“No, Lin Qianyan, you’re a genius. Your life will be very valuable.”","This was the first time Lin Qianyan had ever been affirmed. The person his mother called a genius told him he was one too.","Lin Qianyan was puzzled. “Why are you telling me this?”","Jiang Yinian didn’t answer.","“Because I’m valuable to you, right?”","Lin Qianyan always felt that Jiang Yinian was looking at someone else through him. Jiang Yinian was kind to him because he was using Lin Qianyan as a substitute.","Lin Qianyan soon found out who that person might be: Mu Mian.","During the New Year, Lin Qianyan was taken back to the family home. It was crowded with relatives who had all come together. They all looked at him with disdain, as if he were an idiot. Lin Qianyan ignored them, because in his eyes, they were the fools.","They were slaves to money. Cousin Jiang Yinian told him that once he inherited the Lin Family fortune, these people would become his slaves too.","Lin Qianyan felt sleepy and wanted to go to bed. But there was no room or bed for him in this house. He climbed into Jiang Yun’s wardrobe and decided to sleep there.","Inside the wardrobe, he discovered a hidden drawer. He pulled it open and felt a hard box inside, an old biscuit tin.","When he opened it, he found a stack of photos.","One of the photos showed Jiang Yun holding a baby, smiling happily. The back of the photo had a date and address—this baby wasn’t him.","His mother had another child.","His mother had loved another child.","What value could a baby have? But his mother had smiled at her and lovingly touched her. So unconditional love did exist, just not for him.","Lin Qianyan’s world shattered. All the excuses he had made for Jiang Yun became a joke. Jiang Yun wasn’t incapable of love—she just didn’t love Lin Qianyan.","He was a substitute for Mu Mian, an imperfect tool for inheriting the Lin Family estate.","Lin Qianyan found Jiang Yinian and furiously demanded, “Who is she?”","“Mu Mian. She’s your mother’s child from her previous marriage.”","“Where is she now?”","“Why do you want to find her?”","“To kill her!”","Jiang Yinian warned, “Lin Qianyan, you must not hurt her.”","“Do you love her too? Why does everyone love her? I’ll kill her, chop her up, and throw her into the sea so you’ll never find her!”","At this moment, Lin Qianyan was consumed by anger. It turned out that in Jiang Yinian’s heart, he was just an imperfect substitute too.","“I don’t love Mu Mian, but I love Shen Xiyin. Mu Mian is important to Shen Xiyin, so I won’t allow you to hurt her.”","Lin Qianyan was surprised. He had thought Jiang Yinian was cold and indifferent to everyone. Why would someone like him love someone?","“Lin Qianyan, I was once like you, with no friends. Shen Xiyin was willing to be my friend. She taught me how to get along with the world and showed me what love is. Sadly, her love wasn’t meant for me.”","Lin Qianyan said, “Why don’t you imprison her? Then you’d have her, wouldn’t you?”","“But she wouldn’t be happy. I want her to be happy, even if that means losing her.” Jiang Yinian spoke softly.","Lin Qianyan found Jiang Yinian’s reasoning illogical and foolish. But Jiang Yinian seemed a bit sad at the moment, so he relented, “Fine, I promise you, I won’t kill Mu Mian.”","“Lin Qianyan, do you want to have friends? I can help you.”","“No!”","“Why not?”","“I don’t want to be friends with stupid people. They’re not worthy.”","At Jiang Yinian’s suggestion, Jiang Yun often took him to meet other autistic children, hoping he could befriend them.","Lin Qianyan hated them, as they were even more foolish than normal people.","But Yuanyuan was an exception.","Yuanyuan was also foolish, but he would give Lin Qianyan handmade gifts, ugly though they were, it was the first time someone had ever made him a present.","Lin Qianyan had received many expensive toys before, things he could buy himself with his own money. They weren’t special at all. He hated those gifts.","He didn’t need friends, so he decided Yuanyuan would be his toy, to keep him company in this house. But Yuanyuan refused, wanting to stay with his headmaster mother.","As Lin Qianyan spent more time with Jiang Yinian, he grew even more resentful of his mother. He proposed to Jiang Yinian many times that they kill Jiang Yun. That way, he and Jiang Yinian could take over the entire Lin Family fortune.","With that money, they could do anything they wanted.","He could even abduct Yuanyuan to be his toy.","“Lin Qianyan, you must not kill your mother.” Jiang Yinian rejected his proposal.","“Why not? I don’t need her. She has no value. Why can’t I kill her?”","“Because you’ll regret it.”","That didn’t matter! Later, Li Min persuaded him and Yuanyuan to kill someone. Lin Qianyan was thrilled, acting alongside Li Min while getting Yuanyuan to kill his headmaster mother.","Yuanyuan fell apart, but Lin Qianyan felt even happier. The world didn’t need mothers. Yuanyuan didn’t need one, and neither did he. So he killed Jiang Yun himself.","The knife stabbed into Jiang Yun’s heart again and again, and blood splattered onto his face. But he didn’t feel sad or afraid.","It should have happened long ago. Without this woman, he could live with Jiang Yinian, and he’d have a new family.","Jiang Yinian was the only family member he could accept.","However, when Jiang Yinian learned what he had done, he was extremely angry. \"Lin Qianyan, she is also my relative.\"","Lin Qianyan didn't quite understand Jiang Yinian's reaction. \"Aren't you supposed to be happy? All of the Lin Family's wealth is yours, you've gained so much money. You already have me as a relative, what more do you need? Why not kidnap Mu Mian as well? She's my mother's daughter and also our relative.\"","Lin Qianyan thought, Mu Mian could barely qualify as a decent relative.","Jiang Yinian didn't respond to him. To punish him, Jiang Yinian still had him stay in that mansion, where he remained alone and desolate.","Was he wrong?","No, Jiang Yinian was the one in the wrong. He shouldn't let emotions sway his rationality, as that would make him foolish.","His prediction turned out to be correct. Jiang Yinian, for the sake of his love, had done something even more foolish.","\"Jiang Yinian, she doesn't love you. By doing this, you'll die.\" Lin Qianyan tried to stop his plan.","\"People always die, it's an unchangeable law of nature. But a person's thoughts can continue forever, achieving immortality.\"","Why must people die? Couldn't they just live indefinitely? Those who have no value should die early.","\"Jiang Yinian, I understand now. I am a continuation of your life. I will help you accomplish everything you haven't finished.\"","Jiang Yinian gave him a smile. \"But I don't need you to inherit my legacy. Shen Xiyin said that everything I've done is wrong. So let it end here. Lin Qianyan, your life belongs to yourself.\"","\"But the reason you treat me well is because you thought I would be a qualified heir, isn't it?\" Lin Qianyan knew that Jiang Yinian didn't see him as a relative; he merely needed an heir, and Lin Qianyan just happened to meet the criteria.","Thinking of this, Lin Qianyan couldn't help but envy Mu Mian. She had so much love, while he had none.","This felt so unfair.","But the world is unfair. If you want something, you have to fight for it and seize it, not just wait for fate's gifts.","If Jiang Yinian had imprisoned Shen Xiyin, he would have already possessed love.","\"Lin Qianyan, I treat you well because you remind me of my younger self. But back then, I wasn't so fortunate. Before meeting Shen Xiyin, my world consisted only of myself.\"","Lin Qianyan stared at him with wide eyes, tears slowly welling up in his eyes.","So, he wasn't a substitute for Mu Mian, nor was he just an heir. In Jiang Yinian's heart, he was also a relative.","\"Lin Qianyan, when you fall in love with someone, you'll understand the decision I've made today.\"","\"But I will never fall in love with anyone,\" Lin Qianyan retorted.","\"Then you're both lucky and unlucky.\"","\"Jiang Yinian, will I ever see you again?\"","\"Lin Qianyan, goodbye!\"","Later, Jiang Yinian passed away. Lin Qianyan looked at the body inside the cryogenic chamber and spoke firmly: \"Jiang Yinian, we will meet again!\""]},{"number":222,"title":"Chapter 222: Extra: Everyday Fragments","paragraphs":["(1) Desensitization to Hugs","After three months of effort, Fang Rui and Mu Mian finally managed to hug each other for a staggering three minutes.","But only once.","That one time was because Fang Rui was sick with a cold, lying in bed like a corpse.","However, Fang Rui quickly discovered a bug in Mu Mian's tactile sensitivity—if he pretended to be a corpse, Mu Mian would hug him for a longer time.","But one can't stay still pretending to be a corpse forever.","After a while, Mu Mian noticed Fang Rui's body temperature rising and his heart rate speeding up.","\"Fang Rui, corpses should be cold, but you're too hot!\" Mu Mian complained.","\"......\"","\"Your heart is beating way too fast!\"","\"......\"","\"Fang Rui, why don't you explain yourself?\"","\"Corpses don't talk!\" Fang Rui replied in a hoarse voice.","Later, Mu Mian gradually accepted the \"corpse version\" of Fang Rui—warm and with a heartbeat. Eventually, she accepted the \"living version\" of Fang Rui. In time, she fell in love with the feeling of hugging.","\"Fang Rui, I'm in a bad mood, I need to hug you.\"","\"Fang Rui, Li the Coroner took my corpse, I need to hug you.\"","\"Fang Rui, seeing Officer Zhang made me think of Chen Xue, I need to hug you.\"","Wang and Officer Zhang were speechless, \"Mu Mian, is Fang Rui a human battery? Why do you hug him and instantly feel recharged?\"","Mu Mian's catchphrase became, \"Fang Rui, I'm out of power, I need a recharge.\"","(2) The Birthday Gift","One day, finally, it was Fang Rui's birthday, and Mu Mian presented the long-planned birthday gift.","She wrapped the gift exquisitely, creating a sense of anticipation, but completely impossible to guess what was inside.","Full of anticipation, Fang Rui opened the large box on the table, only to find another beautifully wrapped box inside. He opened that one, only to find another box... After opening five boxes, he finally saw the gift's true face—a plain, unremarkable hourglass.","The design was simple, transparent glass filled with fine, white sand.","\"It's beautiful, the sand inside is especially pure and white,\" Fang Rui complimented it wholeheartedly, then asked, \"What does it symbolize?\"","\"Fang Rui, do you know what an hourglass represents?\"","\"Could the sand inside be diamond dust? Does it symbolize eternal love?\" Fang Rui suddenly felt a sense of foreboding.","Mu Mian corrected him gravely, \"It represents time.\"","\"But it's a countdown.\"","Giving a countdown as a birthday present—wasn't that like a death countdown?","Too inauspicious!","Mu Mian froze for a few seconds, then snatched the hourglass, \"I got it wrong, this isn't the gift, I have to give you a new one!\"","Mu Mian was flustered—it was already so late, all the stores were closed, and she couldn't buy a new gift. What could she give Fang Rui? She couldn't give him a specimen—it would be too distressing.","\"No need for a gift, just give me a kiss.\"","\"But after the kiss, it's over, and there's no evidence that I gave you a gift.\"","\"Then you can kiss me every day.\"","\"Can I kiss you three times? I like the number three more.\"","(3) The Missing Five Corpses on the Resume","One day, Fang Rui suddenly thought of Mu Mian's resume. He asked curiously, \"Did you write that resume yourself?\"","\"Yes, I spent a long, long time writing it. I even left a huge puzzle on it to ensure the chief would definitely hire me.\"","\"What are those five human corpses you didn't list?\"","\"Are you curious?\" Mu Mian asked Fang Rui, \"Come closer, I'll tell you secretly.\"","Fang Rui leaned in to hear her say, \"You're so silly. The other five corpses were mixed-race, so we couldn't tell their ethnicity.\"","\"......\"","(Four) The Pre-Set Baby","A long time later, long after Wang found a new partner and got married, even having a pair of adorable twin babies.","Watching the soft, squishy babies, Mu Mian really wanted to beg Wang to give her a baby.","If it weren't illegal, she might have even considered stealing one.","\"Mu Mian, if you like babies so much, you can have one with Fang Rui,\" Wang suggested.","Mu Mian shook her head, \"No way! What if the baby I have isn't cute?\"","\"No, you two are so good-looking, your baby will definitely be cute.\"","Mu Mian sighed, \"If only we could set the baby's parameters—appearance, personality, gender... all chosen in advance. Wouldn't that be perfect?\"","Fang Rui gently patted her head, interrupting her fantasy, \"That idea is dangerous! What's the difference between that and genetic editing? Besides, if we decide everything about the child, what fun would raising a child be?\"","On their way home, Mu Mian saw an ad: The latest 2029 robot baby is now available... Families, do you want a perfect baby? Hurry and buy one now!","\"Fang Rui.\"","\"Mu Mian, that ad is a scam!\"","\"Buy one.\"","\"Alright.\"","The cost of a robot baby was surprisingly low. Even with rapid advancements in artificial intelligence, commercial robots weren't common. The price was so cheap that it made one suspicious of its authenticity.","Mu Mian placed the order, carefully filling out the robot baby's parameter form, then excitedly awaited its arrival.","Three days later, Mu Mian received a large package, with a beautiful card attached:","【Dear Sister, this is a gift for you, I hope you like it.】","Mu Mian tossed the card aside, then excitedly opened the package, revealing a very cute life-like doll, about a meter tall, dressed in a pretty dress.","It was practically a mini version of Mu Mian.","Mu Mian was very satisfied with its appearance. She charged the robot baby.","After booting up, the robot baby opened its beautiful big eyes and gave a stiff smile, \"Mom, hello, my name is... I don't have a name yet, what should I be called?\"","One day, Mu Mian was watching TV when the robot baby suddenly started dancing around, \"Big news, Author Bug Baby has a new story! Click the homepage to read for free. Everyone, come and check it out...\"","Mu Mian patted the robot baby's head, puzzled, \"Why is it saying such weird things? Has it contracted a virus?\"","Fang Rui said, \"Robot babies aren't reliable, let's have a real baby instead!\"","Suddenly, the sky grew dark, and the lights went out."]}]);
